Justin,Boogaard,Co-Founder & CEO,GoGoGrandparent,"Co-Founder & CEO at GoGoGrandparent: Helping manage millions of rides, meals, meds and more to help at-risk populations live independently and confidently at home.","I believe that the seat of health rests in the home and consider the work we're doing to be good for individuals, communities and the health system. I believe that a system that helps people live their life has the potential to help people live healthier, happier lives. 

I got really lucky and was born into a family that loves me and gives great advice.

I graduated from UCLA in 2011. From 2012 - 2014 I worked on Bubbleboard (http://www.justinboogaard.com/bubbleboard) in a local LA accelerator as an EIR. 

In 2015 I joined Soothe as a Product and Operations Manager & the first hire after the CTO. I built our Customer Service team, managed ops in ten cities and helped the company grow to a $25 million dollar valuation. 

I left to pursue an opportunity I saw in the on demand economy. I hacked things together with my cofounder David Lung and we started gethustle.co. Hustle became a top Kairos company, was voted as one of LA's top 50 companies to watch in 2016 and has been featured in Inc. It was cool, and the best part was I got to learn what a great business partner David is.

Over Christmas my grandmother told me she was afraid of driving at night, and asked for a way to call Uber from her flip phone. GoGoGrandparent was born and she took her first trip to CoCo's Diner. She ordered a stack of buttermilk pancakes and extra crispy bacon.

Now I spend most of my time thinking about ways to help people age better. If you're interested in helping us, you can check our hiring page: https://gogograndparent.com/hiring.

I eat my food in sections, still ask my high school English teacher for book recommendations and do most of my work while listening to nuevo flamenco guitar.",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,San Francisco,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/justinboogaard,GoGoGrandparent,201-500,181,wellness and fitness services,,"GoGoGrandparent's mission is to help people stay healthy and independent as long as possible. Our first product helps older adults use Lyft and Uber without a smartphone. Clients call our number, press 1 and request a car to come to their home. They call our number, press 2 and request a car to pick them up where they were dropped off last or 0 to speak to an operator. 

We help tens of thousands of people around the United States stay independent in their own homes. We've been growing primarily through word of mouth and many, many bingo",https://gogograndparent.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/gogograndparent,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,5000000-10000000,160000,GRANT,gogograndparent.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
