Gary R.,"Cohan, M.D., F.A.C.P.",Founding Chief Medical Officer,Atria Health and Research Institute,"Founding Chief Medical Officer, Atria Health and Research Institute, Beverly Hills, CA","Beverly Hills-based physician Gary R. Cohan, M.D., F.A.C.P. is a board-certified Internist and adult medicine specialist based in Beverly Hills, California. He currently serves as a Founding Chief Medical Officer at the Atria Health and Research Institute, located at 136 S. El Camino Drive in Beverly Hills. At Atria, Dr. Cohan combines his years of visionary clinical expertise and leadership with the most advanced innovations in proactive, preventive care — delivered through a precisely tailored, individualized approach to every patient.Dr. Cohan is board certified in Internal Medicine by the American Board of Internal Medicine. In recognition of his many contributions to the science and practice of medicine and to the community, Dr. Cohan was elected a Fellow of the American College of Physicians (FACP) in 2003.Dr. Cohan received his undergraduate degree in English and Biology (1982) from Amherst College in Massachusetts, did postgraduate research (1983) at Cambridge University in England, and completed his M.D. (1987) at the University of Pennsylvania School of Medicine in Philadelphia.",No,,,,,,United States,California,Beverly Hills,c_suite,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/gary-r-cohan-m-d-f-a-c-p-612b72,Atria Health and Research Institute,201-500,337,hospitals and health care,,"The Atria Health and Research Institute is pioneering a precision-based approach to preventive medicine and longevity. We work at the forefront of leading-edge science and technology, and we believe a collaborative approach to modern preventive medicine can extend healthy life for all.

