Sumit,Aggarwal,President and CEO,Eloxx Pharmaceuticals,"Public and Private co CEO | Ex-McKinsey & Adage Capital |  IIT Kharagpur & Cornell MBA | Biotech, Medtech & Diagnostics |  Company Builder, Commercial Operations | Investor | Transforming Rare Diseases","A strategic leader with a rare dual background in high-conviction healthcare investing (Adage Capital) and top-tier management consulting (McKinsey). My career is defined by the ability to evaluate complex clinical science and execute enterprise-wide turnarounds across the Biotech, MedTech, Life Science Tools, Genomics and Diagnostics sectors.At Eloxx Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ: ELOX), I am leading a comprehensive strategic restructuring and operational pivot. This follows my tenure at Zikani Therapeutics, where I engineered a successful sale to Eloxx, and Progenity, where I managed a 300-person commercial organization and delivered the highest cash flow in company history. To date, I have raised over $250M in equity and debt across the venture and public markets.Combining foundational engineering rigor from IIT Kharagpur with a Cornell MBA, I specialize in bridging the gap between deep science and aggressive commercial value creation. My focus remains on identifying sector-defining catalysts and building resilient, high-growth organizations that deliver life-changing therapies to patients.",No,,,,,,United States,Massachusetts,Greater Boston,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/sumitagg,Eloxx Pharmaceuticals,11-50,12,biotechnology research,,"Eloxx Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company developing novel RNA-modulating drug candidates that are designed to treat rare and ultra-rare premature stop codon diseases. Premature stop codons are point mutations that disrupt protein synthesis from messenger RNA. As a consequence, patients with premature stop codon diseases have reduced or eliminated protein production from the mutation bearing allele accounting for some of the most severe phenotypes in these genetic diseases. These premature stop codons have been identified in over 1,800 rare and ultra-rare diseases. Read-through therapeutic development is focused on extending mRNA half-life and increasing protein synthesis by enabling the cytoplasmic ribosome to read through premature stop codons to produce full-length proteins. Eloxx’s lead product candidate, ELX-02, is a small molecule drug candidate designed to restore production of full-length functional proteins. ELX-02 is in the early stages of clinical development focusing on cystic fibrosis and cystinosis. ELX-02 is an investigational drug that has not been approved by any global regulatory body. Eloxx is headquartered in Waltham, MA, with R&D operations in Rehovot, Israel.",http://www.eloxxpharma.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/eloxx-pharmaceuticals,PUBLIC_COMPANY,0,500000-1000000,94389332,POST_IPO_EQUITY,eloxxpharma.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
