Cindy,Jordan,CEO,Pyx Health,Founder/CEO at Pyx Health: On a mission to improve healthcare quality and outcomes with the power of human connection,"I am the co-founder and CEO of Pyx Health, a tech-enabled member activation company that works with health plans to drive quality health outcomes. Pyx health was founded in 2017 on the mission to improve quality, outcomes and member experience by addressing loneliness and its negative impact on well-being. Today, Pyx Health looks beyond loneliness to members’ and health plans’ evolving needs. Our 2025 acquisition of FarmboxRx - a leading healthcare food company that pioneered fresh fruits and vegetables as a covered health intervention - integrates nutritional support into our tried-and-true care pathways, further strengthening our ability to connect with and motivate members in their own healthcare. And moving our mission another step forward. 

I often say I’m not the idealized ‘start a company from your Harvard dorm room’ entrepreneur. I was a police officer, presidential campaign fundraiser and marketing strategist before I founded my first health IT company - a proprietary referral marketing tool for physicians called Medical Referral Source (MRS) - in the wake of the 2008 recession. When MRS was acquired by The Advisory Board Company in under 4 years, I exited as CEO and continued to work on growing MRS, now known as Crimson Medical Referrals, as managing director for a short time.

In 2017, motivated by our daughter’s struggle with a mental health crisis, my wife (and Pyx co-founder) Anne and I became aware of gaps in healthcare and the pervasive loneliness and social isolation epidemic affecting vulnerable populations. We delved into healthcare research about loneliness only to find that little was being actively done to identify and address the negative mental and physical health effects of loneliness. 

And Pyx Health was born: To focus on identifying and providing support and resources to individuals experiencing the negative health and social effects of loneliness. Our daughter lost her personal battle in 2021 but her memory continues to fuel Pyx’s mission.

What began as a focus on treating loneliness evolved into the ability to impact other potentially deadly barriers to health, and in turn, improve member outcomes for our health plan clients. Pyx Health serves Medicaid and Medicare members from over 70 health plans in nearly 40 states (representing over 6 million covered lives).  Visit www.pyxhealth.com to see for yourself.",No,,,,,,United States,Arizona,Tucson,founder,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/cindy-jordan-66b28863,Pyx Health,51-200,125,hospitals and health care,,"Pyx Health is a tech-enabled member activation company that works with health plans to drive quality health outcomes. Our integrated approach leverages fresh food delivery, real-time care coordination, and personalized resource navigation to address non-medical barriers to care and inspire forward action for members. When people move forward, health plans see measurable return — across quality, utilization, and total cost. 

Pyx sees a 53% higher activation rate in gap closure programs compared to our digital first peers. And as much as 36% decrease in hospitalizations for some high-risk populations. 

While the healthcare system often defaults to engagement through reminders and pings, Pyx Health believes that outreach without meaningful motion serves no one. When we help people overcome the social and behavioral barriers keeping them from optimal health care, they take action, close care gaps, and move their health forward. 

Pyx Health entered the market in 2017 with the laser-focused mission to reduce loneliness as a root cause of myriad physical and behavioral health issues for vulnerable populations. How did we do that? Simply put, we connected: We reached out. We listened. We empathized. And we acted. We learned what these members - who were lonely and disconnected from their support systems - were lacking and we acted to solve their needs. The trust built from that relationship empowers members to be more connected with their health plan and that creates better outcomes for the members AND their plan.

Today, Pyx Health looks beyond loneliness to members’ and health plans’ evolving needs. Our 2025 acquisition of FarmboxRx - a leading healthcare food company that pioneered fresh fruits and vegetables as a covered health intervention - integrates nutritional support into our tried-and-true care pathways, further strengthening our ability to connect with and motivate members in their own healthcare. And moving our mission another step forward.",http://www.pyxhealth.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/pyxhealth,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,5000000-10000000,66704419,PRIVATE_EQUITY,pyxhealth.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
