I have designed Aurion’s scientific strategy and led development efforts including non-clinical development, process development to commercial-scale manufacturing, analytical development, and tech transfer to our manufacturing organizations worldwide.

Aurion has received various biotechnology awards, including the 2022 Prix Galien Top Biotech/Pharma start-up award in recognition for pour impact on patients.

Prior to working at Aurion, I spent 12 years at Novartis, developing cell and gene therapy platforms, including CAR-T, AAV and CRISPR-based therapeutics for a wide range of indications.

I have been fortunate to have key team members follow me as I transitioned from one organization to another over the past 15+ years. Together, we have developed cell therapies, gene therapies and pharmaceuticals. We typically use synthetic biology principles to control molecular pathways, cell behavior and immune responses. Some of our tools of choice include artificial intelligence (AI), genome editing (CRISPR, viral vectors), iPS cells and advanced bioengineering (3D-bioprinting, microfluidics). We also use high-throughput screening and single-cell molecular profiling.

Some of our programs have approached innovation from unconventional angles. For example, we have run experiments on the International Space Station as part of a collaboration involving the Center for Advanced Studies in Space (CASIS), NASA and SpaceX.

I have managed teams in a variety of settings, including very fast-paced, high-stress/high uncertainty environments.

