Reid,Waldman,Chief Executive Officer,Veradermics,Chief Executive Officer at Veradermics,"I founded Veradermics because too many patients and providers have been left with false hope and half-answers to common dermatology and aesthetic conditions, like pattern hair loss. As a board-certified dermatologist with deep clinical experience, I’ve lived the demoralizing experience of level-setting expectations to a mediocre standard of care.  Pattern hair loss is one of the most emotionally impactful conditions I’ve seen while practicing, yet it’s been devoid of innovation for decades. We’ve seen continued flooding of the market with clinically unproven solutions, without any meaningful progress on studied, FDA-approved treatments for nearly 30 years. I’ve watched my patients with pattern hair loss cycle through product after product, searching in mirrors and before and after photos for signs of regrowth, only to feel increasingly defeated every time a treatment fails to meet their expectations. They deserve a solution they can truly count on. At Veradermics, our mission is to set a&nbsp;new standard&nbsp;in pattern hair loss by developing treatments rooted in real evidence.For hair, one solution has risen to the forefront of clinical practice, oral minoxidil, a drug originally developed for high blood pressure in 1979, that reached mainstream status for hair loss after a viral 2022 New York Times article. But, because no one has attempted to maximize it for hair loss, I believe the community is still dealing with seeing limited results; still stuck with all the same expectations, the same searching for few new hairs. Veradermics has set out to turn that false promise into real progress, with a proprietary extended-release formulation that could unlock the true potential of oral minoxidil, intended to give it more time and opportunity to stimulate hair regrowth. My passion for advancing patient care has always driven my work. Before founding Veradermics, I authored over 100 publications and was honored with numerous accolades, including the American Academy of Dermatology’s “Excellence in Patient Care” award. I earned both my Bachelor of Liberal Arts and Medical Degree through the University of Missouri–Kansas City’s 6-Year BA/MD Program and completed my dermatology residency at the University of Connecticut, graduating with “Distinction in Clinical Trials.” When I’m not challenging the industry’s status quo, I’m a certified BBQ judge for the Kansas City Barbecue Society–a nod to my hometown roots and alma mater.",No,,,,,,United States,Connecticut,West Hartford,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/reidwaldman,Veradermics,11-50,43,pharmaceutical manufacturing,,"Veradermics is a late clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company founded by dermatologists with direct clinical experience in the treatment of pattern hair loss, a chronic condition that affects 50 million men and 30 million women in the US alone. 

Our team combines dermatology expertise, clinical research leadership, and biotechnology innovation to advance new solutions and help bring clarity, evidence, and reliability to pattern hair loss.

Our mission: to set a new standard in pattern hair loss by developing treatments rooted in real evidence. 

Our lead investigational product has the potential to be the first non-hormonal oral therapeutic for hair regrowth in men and women. Pattern hair loss is the largest aesthetics condition worldwide, with no new approved prescription therapies in nearly 30 years. 

Learn more at www.veradermics.com",http://www.veradermics.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/veradermics,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,1000000-5000000,,,veradermics.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
