Robert,"Flannery, PhD",CEO,Dr. Robb Farms,"AgTech & Controlled Environment Leader | Applied Agricultural R&D Leader | Plant Biology, Feedstocks, & Carbon Allocation in Crops | Investment, R&D & Growth Strategy | Bridging Science, Operations & Capital","I’m a PhD-trained plant biologist and applied R&D leader working at the intersection of agriculture, innovation, and emerging technology.

Over the past decade, I’ve partnered with corporations, investors, and startups to identify, evaluate, and operationalize new technologies across the agrifood system. My work focuses on translating deep plant biology and systems-level insight into real-world outcomes—supporting product development, commercialization, and long-term sustainability strategies.

As Founder & CEO of Dr. Robb Farms, I raised approximately $40 million to build and scale a data-driven controlled-environment agriculture (CEA) platform that functioned as both a commercial operation and an applied R&D engine. Through this work, I led cross-functional teams of up to 75 people, designed rigorous technology validation and experimental programs, and integrated emerging AgTech solutions into production environments. A consistent theme of this work was understanding how plants allocate carbon under different environmental and management conditions, and leveraging that insight to improve efficiency, yield stability, and resource use—including achieving an approximately 80% reduction in CO₂ inputs through a technology identified during venture diligence.

A significant through-line in my research and applied work is carbon assimilation and allocation within plants. I focus on how biosignaling pathways, environmental conditions, and management strategies influence where plants “invest” carbon into harvestable tissues—insight that directly informs biomass quality, productivity, and suitability for downstream utilization, including bio-based and low-carbon applications.

In parallel, I serve as a Venture Partner and Technical Advisor with Salveo Capital and have held board and advisory roles with organizations including CannaAngels and the California Cannabis Industry Association (CCIA). In these roles, I evaluate early-stage technologies, advise on validation and pilot design, and help organizations assess technical readiness, scalability, and real-world deployment—often at the interface of plant biology, carbon utilization, and sustainability.

My work has been featured in Forbes and includes co-authoring the Cannabis Grower’s Handbook alongside 11 PhDs, translating advanced plant science into practical, scalable production and technology systems.

