Nikej,"Shah, M.D.","Founder, Chairman & CEO",Nirsum Labs,Scientist | Entrepreneur | Investor,"Nirsum Laboratories, Inc. is a CNS-focused clinical-stage biotech company, with lead asset NRS-033 entering Phase 2 clinical development. The drug is an internally discovered, patented, wholly owned, long-acting injectable µ-opioid receptor antagonist – a well validated mechanism of action – being developed for alcohol and opioid use disorder (AUD and OUD, respectively). The US prevalence of AUD is 30mm and  for OUD is 9.4 million.  Both conditions are amongst the largest public health problems in the US. AUD has been a public health problem for decades, worsened by the isolation of the Covid era. The OUD crisis emerged in the early 2000s initiated by prescription opioid overprescribing, now primarily driven by fentanyl abuse. Unfortunately, only three decades-old and problem-laden therapeutics are FDA approved for each of these indications. Those legacy therapeutics have had limited uptake due to low adherence and retention, burdensome side effects, abuse liability, and/or restricted distribution. As a result, AUD and OUD remain severely unmet medical needs, with US therapeutic market penetration into AUD of ~2% and into abstinence-seeking (after detoxification) OUD of ~5%. As a result, relapse rates in AUD and OUD are up to ~60% and ~91%, respectively.

Such dire outcomes reinforce the stigma of addiction as a moral failing, rather than as a treatable biologic disease. Similar misplaced stigmas once prevailed elsewhere in medicine: HIV was initially cast as God’s wrath upon the sinful; major depression was equated to mental infirmity; psychotic patients were once quarantined; and, (even until 2021) obese patients were cast as merely undisciplined. In each case, therapeutic innovation catapulted standards of care out of the dark ages, de-stigmatizing the conditions, revolutionizing outcomes, and driving previously reluctant patients to seek help. Similarly, Nirsum aims to change today’s bleak narrative of addiction to one of hope and recovery.",No,,,,,,United States,New York,New York,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/nikejshah,Nirsum Labs,2-10,7,biotechnology research,,"Nirsum is inventing and developing new medications for opioid use disorder (OUD), the most significant, neglected public health crisis the US has faced in a generation. In cooperation with the National Institutes of Health (HEAL Initiative award UG3DA048234), Nirsum will help lead the fight.  Our message to patients is this: You Can Recover.",http://nirsum.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/nirsum-labs,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,100000-500000,,,nirsum.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
