Jim,Breitmeyer,Board Member,"Vaxart, Inc.","Board Member, Vaxart, Inc.","Dr. James Breitmeyer is a highly qualified pharmaceutical executive and experienced board director.  He has led successful development programs to company acquisitions and eight FDA approvals. His team developed the ADC that was spun out to VelosBio and acquired by Merck & Co for $2.75B, he led the acquisition of Bavarian Nordic Inc's oncology assets by BMS, and was part of the acquisition of Applied Molecular Evolution by Eli Lilly, the acquisition of Zogenix by UCB, and the acquisition of Cadence Pharmaceuticals by Mallinckrodt.  He developed the only agent to be approved by the FDA to increase muscle mass, Serostim® for AIDS related cachexia/sarcopenia.

