Angie,Rowe,President & CEO,Beyond Blindness,President & CEO,"Angie Rowe is an accomplished nonprofit executive and visionary leader dedicated to expanding access, inclusion, and opportunity for children with visual impairments and other disabilities. As President &amp; CEO of Beyond Blindness, she has led a transformational period of growth—doubling revenue from $2.2M to more than $5M, expanding staff from 28 to over 50, and increasing the number of children and families served from 200 to more than 1,500 annually.Under Angie’s leadership, Beyond Blindness has evolved from a traditional vision-focused center to a comprehensive family resource hub, recognized for its pioneering Journey of Care model and its first-of-its-kind partnership with Orange County Head Start. She has cultivated deep partnerships with leading foundations, corporations, and public agencies; advancing both the organization’s mission and its long-term sustainability.Angie is known for her strategic vision, operational discipline, and people-first, servant leadership style. She excels in organizational growth planning, fund development, cross-sector collaboration, and board governance. With a reputation for turning bold ideas into actionable strategies, she builds high-performing teams grounded in optimism, accountability, and shared purpose.Her experience spans over three decades in nonprofit management, fundraising, and community partnership development. Beyond her executive role, she is a statewide advocate for special education and inclusion, serving in leadership roles with the California Association of Special Education Schools and the California Agencies of the Blind &amp; Visually Impaired.",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,Santa Ana,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/angiecianellirowe,Beyond Blindness,11-50,61,individual and family services,,"Beyond Blindness, formerly Blind Children’s Learning Center, is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit with the mission to empower children with visual impairments and other disabilities to achieve their fullest potential. Areas of service include Early Intervention, Education + Enrichment, and Family Support (outlined below), which help children, no matter their abilities, live full and rewarding lives. The Beyond Blindness team embraces a people-first approach and values family, connection, impact, inclusion, stewardship, and optimism.

Early Intervention 
Early Intervention services provide comprehensive support and resources to children ages 0 to 3 to overcome early obstacles, meet key milestones, and establish a foundation for each child to reach their fullest potential. Home-based and center-based services offer vision stimulation and therapy services that help to minimize developmental delays and optimize growth towards an independent future while toddler classrooms, located onsite, focus on healthy development and school readiness. 

Education + Enrichment  
Through Beyond Blindness’ Education + Enrichment services, students receive itinerant (within their public school classroom) education support with a dedicated Teacher of the Visually Impaired (TVI), Orientation & Mobility training (O&M), and the opportunity to attend fun and valuable summer camps. Additional Education + Enrichment services include assistive technology training, peer groups, expanded core curriculum, and life-skills development. 
 
Family Support 
Our Family Support services enable Beyond Blindness to be a resource for families of children with visual impairments and other disabilities throughout the child’s entire journey of care. These services not only offer necessary and comforting support to parents, grandparents, siblings, children and more in the form of education, training and inclusive family events, but they also help provide guidance, a sense of community, and more.",http://www.beyondblindness.org,https://www.linkedin.com/company/beyond-blindness-oc,NON_PROFIT,0,1000000-5000000,,,beyondblindness.org,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
