Morteza,"Naghavi, M.D.","Founder, President & CEO",HeartLung.AI,"Founder and President, HeartLung.AI","Physician–scientist, inventor, entrepreneur, and health technology executive with more than two decades of leadership across academia, nonprofit organizations, and medical technology innovation.

After graduating from Tehran University of Medical Sciences, I was trained at the Texas Heart Institute and University of Texas Health Sciences Houston under late Drs. James T. Willerson and Ward Casscells.

I founded SHAPE – Screening for Heart Attack Prevention and Eradication – which evolved into the Society for Heart Attack Prevention and Eradication (SHAPESociety.org), a nonprofit dedicated to eliminating heart attacks through early detection. My work on vulnerable plaque biology and imaging helped shift cardiovascular medicine from late-stage intervention to identifying high-risk individuals before events occur.

As Executive Chairman of the SHAPE Task Force, I led development of the SHAPE Guidelines advancing coronary artery calcium (CAC) scanning for cardiovascular risk assessment. Our advocacy contributed to passage of Texas HB1290, the first U.S. law mandating insurance coverage for CAC screening. I am currently leading efforts to secure CMS reimbursement for CAC nationwide.

I have led major international consensus publications, including the highly cited “From Vulnerable Plaque to Vulnerable Patient” series redefining cardiovascular risk assessment, and edited Asymptomatic Atherosclerosis: Pathophysiology, Detection and Treatment.

In response to the Google–AHA $50M “One Brave Idea” challenge, I led the Machine Learning Vulnerable Patient Project to develop an AI-enabled system forecasting near-term heart attack risk. More recently, I launched an initiative to develop a fully automated robotic ultra–low-dose CT platform for preventive screening outside healthcare settings.

I hold 30+ patents and have founded multiple medical technology companies. I was an early cofounder of Volcano Corporation (NASDAQ: VOLC), later acquired by Philips. My invention, Digital Thermal Monitoring of Endothelial Function (VENDYS), is an FDA-cleared technology that received $1 million award as a top emerging medical technologies in Texas.

I am Founder and Executive Chairman of HeartLung.AI, advancing AI-enabled detection of cardiovascular disease, lung cancer, COPD, osteoporosis, and cardiometabolic disorders using low-dose chest CT. In 2023, HeartLung’s AI platform received FDA Breakthrough Device designation.

My mission is to transform healthcare from reactive sick-care to proactive, AI-enabled preventive care at scale, including underserved and developing countries.",No,,,,,,United States,Texas,San Francisco Bay Area,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/morteza-naghavi-m-d-4b659721,HeartLung.AI,11-50,14,wellness and fitness services,,"Focusing on preventing heart attack and lung cancer with supervised AI, mobile app, and noninvasive imaging. HeartLung received FDA Breakthrough Designation for AI-CAC™ that detects signs of heart disease in CT scans more accurately than humans.",https://www.heartlung.ai,https://www.linkedin.com/company/heartlung,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,,,heartlung.ai,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
