I’m now the Co-Owner and CMO, working with my husband and many other members of our family to carry forward the mission that my grandfather started.

We now reach thousands of healthcare practitioners, retail partners, and everyday people who are committed to optimizing their health, starting with the most foundational element – the cell.

Most days, I think of myself as a translator.

I take decades of research on cell membranes, minerals, and foundational nutrition and turn it into something the average person can actually understand and use. Because science only matters if it helps real people make better choices.

Here's what I've learned so far…

Most wellness advice skips the foundation. 

It jumps to protocols, supplements, and quick fixes before addressing what your cells actually need to function.

We take a different approach. We don’t sell first, we teach first. 

We believe education builds more trust than any ad campaign ever could. That philosophy has helped us grow from a practitioner-focused brand into partnerships with values-aligned retailers like Erewhon and Thrive Market — all while staying true to who we are.

I’m here to talk about cellular health, women's wellness, and what it takes to build a brand that leads with education instead of hype. One that’s been in my family for three generations and counting.

If you're a health-conscious consumer trying to understand why you feel “off,” a practitioner looking for a supplement brand that matches your standards, or a marketer curious about education-first growth, you're in the right place.

