Nate,Thomas,Chief Executive Officer,Shmoody,Founder @ Shmoody | Asking for help isn’t weakness - it’s strength,"I spent years in law and finance before realizing my real work was elsewhere.

I struggled with mental health. That struggle gave me a responsibility - and an opportunity - to help others.

Now I'm Co-founder and CEO of Shmoody, a mental health app and platform built to be human and engaging. We've grown to 1.5M+ users and instituional partnerships with universities like Duke, Texas Tech, and three HBCUs because we do something different: we meet people where they are.

No lectures. No clinical jargon. Just real tools that help students feel better today and grow into who they want to become tomorrow.

We use human-centered design, behavioral science, and yes - humor. Because if mental health tools feel like homework, people won't use them. And if they don't use them, we're not actually helping anyone.

