Maxwell,C.,Founder/CEO,PeelAways ~ Eliminating 2 a.m. Sheet Changes for Exhausted Caregivers,"Inventor of Peelaways | Making Aging and Caregiving Easier, One Bed at a Time. | Turning 2:17 a.m. from Crisis to Non-Event | Shark Tank Alum","In the 1950s, the disposable diaper changed the world. It broke the ""wash-boil-scrub"" cycle that tethered parents to the laundry room.

Today, we are facing a different hygiene crisis - but the solution is the same.

As the inventor of Peelaways, I am applying that ""disposable revolution"" to the greatest challenge of our time: Aging in Place. We are currently losing the battle against caregiver burnout. Families aren't choosing nursing homes because they want to; they are being forced into them by the ""Incontinence Cliff.""

The ""Laundry Ordeal"" is the Breaking Point. Current clinical advice for managing soiled reusable bedding and pads requires a grueling process: manual solid waste removal, cold-water pre-rinsing, chemical soaking, and high-heat sanitization of both the linens and the washing machine.

When this happens 3x a day, and in the middle of the night.. the caregiver breaks. When the caregiver breaks, the ""Age in Place"" dream ends.

The Economic Impact of a 60-Second Peel:

For Families: With private nursing home rooms costing $11,294/month in 2026, delaying placement by just one quarter saves families over $30,000.

For the Taxpayer: Peelaways provides the ""micro-efficiency"" that prevents the $135,000/year per-patient cost from shifting to the government (Medicaid).

For the Care Economy: We protect the 63 million unpaid caregivers in the U.S. from back injuries and sleep deprivation.

I am dedicated to the Logistics of Dignity. We turn a 90-minute sanitation ordeal into a 60-second ""peel.""

Let’s connect if you believe it’s time to modernize eldercare for the 21st century.",Yes,,,,,,United States,New York,New York,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/maxwell-cohenpal,PeelAways ~ Eliminating 2 a.m. Sheet Changes for Exhausted Caregivers,2-10,6,hospitals and health care,,"Peelaways is a simple, practical solution designed for one of the hardest parts of caregiving: changing a bed after an accident.

Caregivers deal with incontinence every day. Traditional sheets, pads, and mattress protectors make bed changes slow, physical, and exhausting. They require lifting, stripping the bed, extra laundry, and repeated patient handling. Over time, this leads to caregiver strain, patient discomfort, and real safety risks.

Peelaways was created to make this moment easier.

Peelaways is a fitted bed sheet with multiple soft, disposable layers. Each layer is 100 percent waterproof. When a layer becomes soiled, it can be peeled away to reveal a clean sheet underneath. The bed can be reset in under 60 seconds, even while someone remains in bed.

For caregivers, this means less lifting, less laundry, and less physical strain.
For patients, it means less disruption, more comfort, and greater dignity.
For care teams, it means cleaner beds, protected mattresses, and more efficient use of time.

Peelaways is used in homecare, hospice, assisted living, pediatric care, and other clinical and non-clinical settings. It helps caregivers manage incontinence safely and efficiently while supporting aging in place and quality of care.

