Mark,Connell,Co-Founder & President,SLBST Pharma,Working to improve the health of women at SLBST Pharma as Co-Founder & President,"I enjoy challenges and I get things done. I find solutions where others often don't see them. Here are a few stories:

As a 19-year-old college student on a gap year, I made my way from the Andes to the southeast corner of Columbia on the banks of the Amazon River, where I hopped small boats from town to town traveling 2,000 miles downriver passing Benjamin Constant, Manaus, and Santarem, to reach the port of Belem on the Atlantic. From there I traveled overland south to Rio de Janeiro, where I convinced the captain of a German freighter, heading to New York City, to hire me as a crew member for the voyage.

While operating a sports nutrition company, I organized a charity 5K road race to support Sole Train, a running program for kids in the Boston Public Schools. The City of Boston resisted the disruptions caused by a new road race along city streets and made approval difficult. We almost got derailed in our first year as we were the first road race held in the city following the Boston Marathon Bombing. Over the course of a decade, we raised hundreds of thousands of dollars to support youth educational programs.

I had been a lifelong endurance athlete, completing eight marathons and multiple triathlons. Despite serious training, I remained a middle-of-the-pack runner, priding myself more on my persistence than my finish times. One day, while lifting weights as cross training, a trainer remarked that I had good form and suggested that I enter a powerlifting competition.  I laughed but took his suggestion and I’ve never looked back. The shift from endurance sports to strength & power was a revelation that played to my innate athletic capacities. I’m now a nationally competitive powerlifter, have been the USAPL Northeast Region champion, and hold multiple state records.",No,,,,,,United States,Florida,Greater Boston,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/markgconnell,SLBST Pharma,2-10,9,biotechnology research,,"SLBST Pharma is developing a non-hormonal therapy to treat endometriosis, a broadly prevalent disease with no cure and no effective therapies. We’ve identified a known immunomodulator, with a strong safety record, that shows promise in clinical studies as the first effective treatment for endometriosis. We have a green light from FDA to proceed with a Phase 2 dose-finding study. We hold issued and pending patents protecting this novel indication.

Patients are desperate for better treatment options. Over 4M women have been diagnosed with endometriosis, with two-thirds reporting significant functional impairment. There is no cure and current treatment options are bleak, skewing toward surgery and heavy use of opioids: three-quarters of patients undergo surgery (with nearly half opting for hysterectomy), one-third of patients take opioids, and one-in-ten patients take GnRH analogues, which chemically induce menopause. These options are expensive and none provide effective relief from the pain of endometriosis.

We've developed a reformulation of the well-known immunomodulator hydroxychloroquine (HCQ) that addresses endometriosis pathology at two points. It reduces pain by normalizing chronic inflammation and it inhibits lesion formation by reducing autophagy. Inflammation drives both pain sensitization and fibrosis, which causes adhesions. We’ve asked FDA to be indicated for relief of pain, as this is an established approval pathway which will allow us to get to market quickly.",https://www.slbstpharma.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/slbst-pharma,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,,,slbstpharma.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
