Tomo,Marjanovic,Chief Executive Officer,Aspire Rejuvenation Clinic,"Founder, Aspire Rejuvenation Clinic | Building the clinical standard for cellular longevity medicine | Author, Operation Optimal","I went from law enforcement to building one of the country’s most clinically rigorous longevity medicine companies. The throughline isn’t as strange as it sounds.After years on the job watching what chronic disease, stress, and systemic neglect do to people, including the men and women I served alongside, I became convinced that the American healthcare system wasn’t broken. It was just built for the wrong question. It was designed to manage disease, not optimize the human running underneath it.So in 2019, I founded Aspire Rejuvenation Clinic to build the standard I couldn’t find as a patient.Today, Aspire is a multi-state longevity and preventative medicine company specializing in hormone optimization, peptide therapy, regenerative medicine, medical weight loss, and IV wellness. We operate across five U.S. locations, Pittsburgh, Orlando, Dallas, Ebensburg PA, and Cleveland, with international expansion underway in Dubai, Canada, South Africa, and Eastern Europe. We see patients nationwide via telemedicine, with a franchise model launching in late 2026.What separates Aspire isn’t the menu. It’s the methodology.Most longevity clinics sell single tools such as TRT, peptides, IV drips, as if any one of them is a complete answer. Aging is twelve cellular mechanisms working against you simultaneously. Treating one is a service. Treating the system is medicine.That’s what we built. The Cellular Longevity Protocol, Aspire’s flagship clinical framework, addresses five mechanism-driven pillars: endocrine optimization, mitochondrial biogenesis, mitochondrial membrane optimization, NAD+ restoration, and tissue repair. Coordinated. Monitored quarterly. Refined with each patient over time. It’s the protocol I personally run, and the standard I hold every Aspire provider to.Recognition