Yitzy,Halon,Chief Executive Officer,Mainspring Recovery,CEO @ Mainspring Recovery,"As the Co-Founder of Mainspring Recovery, I am passionate about building innovative solutions that bridge the gap between individuals in need and the care they deserve. At Mainspring, we’re committed to redefining substance abuse treatment by combining evidence-based practices with a deep understanding of the human experience, ensuring that recovery is not just a possibility, but a sustainable reality.

With a vision for accessible and transformative care, I’ve dedicated my career to fostering programs and facilities that prioritize both clinical excellence and compassionate support. From navigating the complexities of healthcare operations to developing scalable systems for long-term impact, I thrive on creating environments where people and organizations can succeed together.",No,,,,,,United States,Maryland,Baltimore,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/yitzy-halon-15a271a9,Mainspring Recovery,51-200,50,mental health care,,"The name “Mainspring” was chosen with intention and meaning. In a mechanical watch, the mainspring is the central source of power. It is the tightly wound spring that stores energy and releases it gradually, keeping every gear, hand, and movement working in harmony. Without it, the watch cannot function and time itself appears to stand still. In much the same way, Mainspring Recovery was founded on the belief that healing begins when a person reconnects with their own inner source of movement, resilience, and life. That moment of reconnection is where healing truly starts.

With this philosophy at its core, founder Yitzy Halon envisioned creating a place that reflected both restoration and possibility. His goal was to design an environment where individuals seeking recovery could experience dignity, structure, and peace while rebuilding their lives. Recovery requires more than treatment alone; it requires an atmosphere that encourages hope, stability, and human connection.

After an extensive search for the right location, Yitzy discovered a former Sleep Inn hotel in Dumfries, Virginia. The property offered the opportunity to transform an existing structure into something entirely new—a residential treatment center designed to support individuals on their recovery journey. In March of 2022, construction began to convert the hotel into what would become Mainspring’s flagship 74-bed residential treatment facility.

By December 2022, the transformation was complete. Just a few months later, in March 2023, Mainspring received its license from the Virginia Department of Behavioral Health and Developmental Services, officially opening its doors to individuals seeking treatment and support.

The vision did not stop there. In 2025, Yitzy expanded Mainspring’s mission by revitalizing the historic Court Street property in Lynchburg, Virginia. Once a vital community resource that had closed its doors, the building was restored and reopened to serve the residents of Lynchburg.",http://mainspringrecovery.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/mainspring-recovery,PARTNERSHIP,0,1000000-5000000,,,mainspringrecovery.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
