Adam,"Watson, PhD",Co-Founder & CEO,MeCo Diagnostics,CEO at MeCo Diagnostics | Board Member at American Cancer Society,"I'm a cancer biologist building tools to enable a new modality of high-value, low-toxicity cancer therapy. Over the last 10 years, my team and I have developed the first clinically validated predictive biomarker for antifibrotic therapy. While I was in grad school, my aunt was diagnosed with advanced cancer. Despite having ""excellent"" health insurance, her treatments cost over $100K in out-of-pocket expenses. Even the best health insurance is not the shield we expect it to be when we need it the most, for one heartbreaking reason: families of patients with advanced cancer are often driven by desperation to seek out non-reimbursable treatments when all else has failed, only to find themselves drowning in debt in the wake of grief and loss.Cancer isn’t just a health problem—it’s a growing economic problem. Expensive new therapies are merely transforming the former into the latter, since cancer debts can now outlive cancer patients by years or decades. Unbelievably, the price for newly launched oncology drugs is now ~$300,000/year, up from $64,000/year in 2012. As a result, payers are under pressure and passing along the cost to patients—nearly half of American patients with advanced breast cancer are currently being chased by debt collectors due to mounting medical debt. Fortunately, the MeCo Score was recently validated as the first predictive biomarker test to harness an FDA-approved, generic antifibrotic drug, which costs pennies on the dollar compared to any other targeted therapy for breast cancer. Moreover, it is well-tolerated by patients and has a favorable safety profile.In our landmark Phase 2 trial, High MeCo Score patients who received antifibrotic therapy vs standard-of-care experienced a 62% reduction in risk of recurrence over 9.7 years on average. The magnitude of this result is unprecedented in early-stage breast cancer. Patients who may benefit can only be matched using the MeCo Score test, which has been evaluated in 4 studies comprised of nearly 4000 patients, in collaboration with Cleveland Clinic, Mayo Clinic, George Washington University, UArizona, and the Spanish National Cancer Research Center. Our enabling research has been published in high-impact journals: Cell, Science, Cancer Cell, Cell Reports, Nature Communications, Clinical Cancer Research, etc.We are venture-backed and harness 100+ years of combined experience in diagnostics and therapeutics. Join our mission to save patients’ lives and livelihoods, simultaneously.",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,San Diego,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/adam-watson-phd,MeCo Diagnostics,2-10,9,biotechnology research,,"We are a venture-backed startup with the only clinically validated biomarker test to match breast cancer patients with antifibrotic therapy—a breakthrough targeted therapy that represents a fundamentally new way to treat breast cancer.

MeCo Diagnostics traces its origins to the oldest observation in cancer biology: tumors often grow stiffer than surrounding tissue, due to fibrosis, which produces a palpable lump. However, not all cancer cells are responsive to fibrotic stiffness, but those that are become “mechanically conditioned,” programmed to wreak havoc as they spread throughout the body.

Fortunately, there are both old and new antifibrotic drugs that can be repurposed/repositioned to deprogram these dangerous cancer cells. This serendipity has empowered us to develop a commercially viable, biomarker-enabled drug repurposing/repositioning approach to augment standard-of-care chemotherapy. 

Our landmark Phase 2 randomized controlled trial demonstrated the greatest long-term survival benefit ever reported for a targeted therapy in the history of breast oncology: 

Antifibrotic therapy resulted in a 62% reduction in risk of recurrence over 9.7 years for High MeCo patients specifically, while Low MeCo patients experienced no benefit.

The MeCo Score has been rigorously evaluated in 4 studies, comprised of >4000 patients in total. We have collaborated/published with oncologists at Cleveland Clinic, Mayo Clinic, George Washington University, USC, University of Arizona, the Swiss Federal Institute of Technology (ETH), and the Spanish National Cancer Research Center (CNIO). 

Moreover, since MeCo Score can match patients with a generic-emergent drug, the cost of targeted antifibrotic therapy will soon be >10X cheaper than any other targeted therapy for patients with certain high-risk tumors.

Patients benefit from improved survival, and patients/payers benefit from dramatically reduced treatment costs—a rare win-win opportunity.

Join our mission...",http://www.mecodiagnostics.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/meco-diagnostics,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,1000000,PRE_SEED,mecodiagnostics.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
