Teri,Frykenberg RN CCM BCPA,Founder/Owner,Nurse Advocate Entrepreneur,Founder/Owner @ Nurse Advocate Entrepreneur | RN Patient Advocate and advocate for patients and  nurses who are suffering in the modern healthcare system and know they deserve better.,"I’m Teri (Dreher) Frykenberg, RN, CCM, BCPA — Board-Certified Patient Advocate, nurse entrepreneur, author, newspaper columnist, public speaker, and founder of Nurse Advocate Entrepreneur, where I train and equip nurses to step out of burnout and into their calling as independent patient advocates and business owners.

After more than 30 years in critical care, a pivotal moment changed my life. In 2010, I was nearly fired for standing up for a patient whose life was in danger. That experience opened my eyes to a harsh truth: it was no longer safe for nurses to advocate freely within a system driven by profit and fear.

So, I walked away from the bedside — and built something better. I founded North Shore Patient Advocates, one of the nation’s first nurse-led advocacy firms. For over a decade, my team helped families navigate complex medical challenges and reclaim their voice in the healthcare system. In 2024, I sold the company to focus fully on empowering other nurses to do the same.

Through Nurse Advocate Entrepreneur, I now train and mentor nurses and doctors on how to launch and grow advocacy practices that serve patients with compassion, integrity, and freedom — while reigniting their passion for nursing and medicine.

As a national speaker and conference presenter, I’m passionate about inspiring healthcare professionals to lead with courage, integrity, and heart — and to become the advocates our system so desperately needs.

Because here’s what I believe to my core:
💥 Healthcare isn’t just broken — it’s burning out the healers.
💥 Patients deserve advocates who truly care.
💥 Nurses deserve to lead the change — not be silenced by the system.

