Kristine,Hoestermann,Head of Mental Wellness,Cabana,"Mental Health Tech Leader | Founder @RARE. | Clinical Programs, Content & AI-Informed Products | MSW, LICSW | Building human-centered systems that see the individual and scale with care","My work in mental health has always been about building care that holds up in real life—not just in theory.

I began my career as a clinical social worker, working across child welfare, education, and community-based settings. Those early years shaped how I show up professionally—creative, grounded, and deeply committed to meeting people where they are. Over time, my work evolved from direct care into building the systems that support care at scale.

Several years into my career, I began experiencing symptoms of what was later identified as a very rare disease. I didn’t “look sick,” but my body and mind were navigating something deeply destabilizing. That experience—of being unseen, isolated, and unsure how to communicate what was happening—fundamentally changed how I think about mental health, visibility, and access.

Out of that space, I founded RARE., a mission-driven brand built to start conversations and bring invisible struggles into the light. What began as a personal response grew into a broader commitment: designing tools, content, and communities that help people feel seen, validated, and less alone.

Today, I lead mental health programs, content, and product-adjacent initiatives across live, asynchronous, and AI-supported experiences. My work focuses on translating clinical integrity and lived insight into practical frameworks, ethical guardrails, and scalable systems—so care remains human, even as it grows.

