Gilmer,Valdes,Chief Executive Officer,OncoBrain (Formerly The BlueScrubs),"Chief Executive Officer, Founder @ OncoBrain | Developing Deterministic Clinical Reasoning.","I’m the Founder and CEO of OncoBrain Inc., where we are building the clinical reasoning and treatment planning layer for oncology. Our aim is to make oncologic decision-making more explicit, reproducible, and actionable by helping care teams generate guideline-concordant, patient-specific plans and operationalize their execution across diagnostics, referrals, authorizations, scheduling, and care logistics. In practice, this means translating expert reasoning into care pathways that can be delivered reliably in the real world.

Previously, I served as Vice Chair of Machine Learning and Head of Clinical AI at Moffitt Cancer Center, where I led the translation of machine learning research into deployed clinical workflows. I also co-developed BlueScrubs, the clinician-facing AI platform that evolved into OncoBrain. That work established the principles that continue to define our approach: transparency, safety constraints, measurable clinical endpoints, and workflow-native integration.

My work sits at the intersection of medical physics, clinical oncology, and machine learning. I earned my PhD in Medical Physics from UCLA, completed clinical residency and fellowship training in Therapeutic Medical Physics at the University of Pennsylvania, served on faculty at UCSF, and pursued AI research through an NIH K08 across UCSF, UC Berkeley, and Stanford. My early research focused on machine learning and advanced statistical modeling for quality assurance, outcome prediction, and treatment personalization, particularly in prostate and lung cancer, with an emphasis on robustness under real-world clinical data constraints.

Scientifically, I have contributed to the development of Expert-Augmented Machine Learning and interpretable modeling frameworks, including work spanning MediBoost, Conditional Super Learner, Representational Gradient Boosting, and additive tree-based methods. I have received federal grant support and serve as PI on two awarded patents.

At the center of my work is a simple belief: the future of oncology AI must make clinical reasoning visible, trustworthy, and actionable at the point of care.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Florida,Tampa,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/gilmer-valdes-02066725,OncoBrain (Formerly The BlueScrubs),2-10,11,hospitals and health care,,"OncoBrain was created to address a systemic problem in cancer care: the growing gap between rapidly evolving oncology evidence and real-world clinical decision-making.

Medical knowledge now doubles every 73 days. Oncology guidelines update hundreds of times each year. Yet most cancer care is delivered outside academic medical centers, where clinicians are asked to make high-stakes, patient-specific decisions without consistent access to subspecialty expertise or the time required to synthesize complex evidence in real time.

The challenge is no longer access to information. It is translating that information into confident, guideline-concordant decisions at the point of care.
Our mission is to ensure that the future of medical AI is built not behind closed doors, but in open collaboration with the physicians and researchers who understand patients best. On Blue Scrubs, clinicians can ask complex clinical questions, engage in AI-powered discussions, evaluate and rank different medical AI models, and collaborate in real time to refine their reasoning and performance.

Each interaction—every question, comparison, or clinical debate—feeds into a continuous feedback loop that trains AI systems to think more like experienced clinicians. This growing body of physician-aligned intelligence powers The Blue Scrubs Dataset, a 25-billion-token open medical corpus designed to evolve with every new contribution from the global medical community.

By opening access to both the tools and the data that shape medical AI, Blue Scrubs transforms how intelligence in medicine is created, shared, and improved. Together, clinicians and AI researchers are building a new kind of collective intelligence—one that learns from the world’s best medical minds to create the next generation of trustworthy, domain-specialized AI physicians.",https://oncobrain.ai,https://www.linkedin.com/company/oncobrain,NON_PROFIT,0,500000-1000000,,,oncobrain.ai,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
