Abby,Krage,"Co-Founder, Head of Strategy & Growth",Tyrian,"Co-Founder, Tyrian | TGUARD™ for Long-Term Care | Non-Antibiotic UTI Support for SNFs & Assisted Living | Antibiotic Stewardship Programs","Advancing UTI Care in Long-Term Care — Without Antibiotics

As Co-Founder of Tyrian, I lead strategy, sales, and commercial partnerships for TGUARD™, our clinically studied, Aronia-based supplement designed to support urinary tract health in skilled nursing facilities and assisted living communities.

Why It Matters
UTIs are among the most frequent and costly challenges in long-term care. They strain nursing staff, drive unnecessary antibiotic use, and put vulnerable residents at risk. With TGUARD™, we offer a science-backed, antibiotic-free approach designed to support healthier urinary function and complement existing infection management programs.

What We Offer LTC Facilities
- Clinically studied urinary health support for high-risk resident populations
- A non-antibiotic approach that aligns with antibiotic stewardship goals
- Practical integration into SNF and ALF care protocols
- A cost-conscious solution that supports reducing unnecessary interventions and hospital visits

The Story Behind the Science
Tyrian was co-founded by Dr. Steven Saulsbury, MD, an interventional radiologist and researcher who dedicated years to studying Aronia berry's role in urinary tract health. He was a brilliant clinician, a tireless advocate for nature-backed medicine, and my mentor. He built the scientific foundation that TGUARD™ stands on. After his passing in 2022, his son and I took the reins, committed to carrying his work forward with the same rigor and purpose he instilled in us.

Let's Connect
If you're exploring non-antibiotic UTI support for your residents, building out an antibiotic stewardship program, or looking for a science-backed addition to your care protocols, I'd love to talk.
