Dan,"Turner, PhD","Vice President, Athlete Safety & Performance",Enhanced,"VP, Athlete Safety & Performance @ Enhanced Games|| Building ecosystems for ambitious humans to integrate biology, identity & agency || Founder • Scientist • Consultant","My work sits at the intersection of performance science, institutional design, and human development. Over the past 15+ years, I’ve spent time alongside individuals and teams operating at a very high level — from Olympians and extreme sports athletes to surgeons, musicians & artists, coaches and other professionals working in complex, high-stakes environments. That proximity has shaped how I think.

Over time, I’ve become less interested in performance in isolation, and more drawn to a broader question: Why do highly capable and ambitious people — established or unseen — lose their clarity, their energy, or their sense of direction? I’ve seen how easily ambition can become misaligned with health, identity, and long-term trajectory — especially in modern day environments that demand a lot but offer little integration.

My focus now is on designing ecosystems that help ambitious people bring those elements back into alignment — integrating biology, identity, and agency so that ambition can mature rather than quietly erode. I currently work at the frontier of human performance and medical governance through my role with Enhanced Games, which continues to inform the broader systems and technology I’m building beyond sport.

