Russell,Medford,Chairman of the Board,OncoSpherix,"Chairman and CEO, Covanos, Inc.","Russell M. Medford, MD, PhD is Chairman and CEO of Covanos, Inc and a senior biotechnology executive with extensive private and public company experience as Chief Executive Officer and Board member of multiple biotechnology and other health related companies, organizations and research institutes. He has had extensive experience leading companies and organizations engaged in comprehensive therapeutic drug research and development, developing multiple, novel, first-in-man clinical candidates for the treatment of cardiovascular disease, diabetes and arthritis and has executed multiple strategic partnerships with major pharmaceutical  companies. He has extensive experience in both the private and public financial markets including initial public offerings (IPO) raising over $500 million for corporate, clinical development and research programs and returning over $2.5 billion in shareholder value.  He currently serves as a Board member of ThermoGenesis Holdings (Nasdaq:THMO), engaged in the research, development, and commercialization of advanced technologies for cellular therapies and delivery systems for use in regenerative medicine and has served on multiple public and  private company Boards. He is a board-certified physician, an inaugural Fellow of the Council on Basic Cardiovascular Sciences of the American Heart Association, and has held faculty positions at Harvard Medical School and the Emory University School of Medicine. He is a past Chairman of the Center for Global Health Innovation and Global Health Crisis Coordination Center, past Chairman and current member of the External Advisory Board for the Petit Institute of Bioscience and Bioengineering of the Georgia Institute of Technology, and a serves as Chairman of the Board of Directors for the Global Center for Medical Innovation.",No,,,,,,United States,Georgia,Atlanta,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/russell-medford-9579b517,OncoSpherix,2-10,6,biotechnology research,,"OncoSpherix, Inc., based in Atlanta, Ga, is a pre-clinical stage oncology drug development company that is advancing a proprietary platform of first-in-class small molecule therapeutics that are designed to improve the quality of life and survival for people with many forms of cancer by targeting a common feature of solid tumors: the activation of hypoxia inducible factor-1 (HIF-1). Nearly all solid cancers grow faster than their blood supply, leading to regions of low oxygen in the tumors and HIF activation. The HIFs in turn induce the expression of over 100 genes that help tumor cells survive and spread. OncoSpherix has several classes of small molecules that block activation of HIF-1 through novel mechanisms. OncoSpherix’s lead clinical candiate has been shown in mouse models to reduce primary tumor growth, inhibit metastases, and prolong survival in many types of cancer (glioblastoma, pancreatic cancer, uveal melanoma, lung cancer, breast cancer). Importantly, the agents are well tolerated and can be combined with therapeutics that work in well oxygenated regions of cancers, leading to dramatically enhanced cancer control.",http://www.oncospherix.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/oncospherix,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,100000-500000,2917189,GRANT,oncospherix.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
