Specialties: Strategic planning and implementation",No,,,,,,United States,Michigan,Lansing,founder,"c_suite, consulting",https://www.linkedin.com/in/tim-colonnese-446b743,Peptinovo Biopharma,2-10,10,biotechnology research,,"Chemotherapy is the cornerstone of cancer treatment, but its effectiveness is often limited by severe side effects, such as nerve damage or reduced white blood cell counts. These and other debilitating side effects can force dose reductions or treatment discontinuations, impacting a patient's chances of survival.

Peptinovo Biopharma, Inc. has developed a patented drug-delivery platform called PALM™ (US #10,532,105), which is designed to specifically target cancer cells while protecting healthy tissues. Peptinovo aims to improve the effectiveness of proven chemotherapy drugs while significantly minimizing, and potentially eliminating, harmful side effects to the patient.

Cancer cells rely on specific nutrient pathways to absorb cholesterol, which fuels their rapid growth. The PALM™ platform mimics a cholesterol carrier (HDL), and like a ""Trojan horse,” it delivers chemotherapy drugs directly into cancer cells by disguising them as nutrients. 

Our lead drug candidate is PALM™ + Paclitaxel, a first-line therapeutic used for over 30 years to treat many cancers such as breast, ovarian, lung, prostate, and pancreatic. Extensive animal trials demonstrate that PALM + chemotherapy significantly reduces, and often eliminates, the harmful side effects from the chemotherapy. 

Peptinovo’s smart drug delivery platform could unleash chemotherapy’s full potential - with the aim to be effective and safer for patients worldwide.",https://peptinovo.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/peptinovo-biopharma,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,,,peptinovo.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
Michelle,"May MD, CSP",CEO,Am I Hungry? Mindful Eating Programs and Training,"Harness the power of vibrant well-being through mindful eating, joyful movement, and intentional self-care. Am I Hungry? Workshops | Retreats | Training | Keynotes | Books | Digital Tools.","Everyone craves a personal and professional life they feel enthusiastic about. My “students” learn a mindful decision-making model based on awareness, curiosity, and micro-actions to live more balanced, productive, joyful, vibrant lives.

My passion for vibrant living and mindful eating stems from my 20+ year struggle with food and body image. Despite earning a medical degree, completing a Family Medicine Residency, and sustaining a busy medical practice and family, I continued to waste time, money, and energy on yo-yo dieting.

I discovered that many of my patients were struggling too, and that the conventional approach to health doesn’t lead to lasting change.

I created Am I Hungry?® Mindful Eating Programs and Training in 1999 to change the way the world thinks about eating. Am I Hungry? is a novel wellness program that employs mindfulness-based, non-diet, weight-inclusive strategies to identify and resolve the mindless and emotional eating habits that sabotage most attempts at sustainable lifestyle change. We offer experiential mindful eating workshops, retreats, and corporate wellness programs. We have trained over 800 health and wellness professionals in over 40+ countries to offer mindful eating programs, coaching, and therapy in their communities, practices, and workplaces.

I have written 12 books, workbooks, and training manuals, including the book series, ""Eat What You Love, Love What You Eat.” Perhaps this comment from one reader explains why I love to do this work: “You have successfully upended the diet industry and diet culture, exposing how the model is destructive to most people because it exacerbates a vicious cycle of self-loathing. Am I Hungry? has been central to healing my food and self-esteem issues, and after years of trying every other diet and exercise plan, it is the only one that has helped instead of hurting.”

As an inspirational wellness speaker and Certified Speaking Professional, my interactive virtual and in-person keynotes and workshops deliver paradigm-shifting, yet practical strategies to promote a healthier, vibrant, productive workplace and community. I bring my personal and professional insights, humor, and authenticity to the stage to offer a compelling, constructive, and sustainable path to optimal well-being.

I also enjoy working with the media to counter conventional restrictive, weight-focused approaches to eating, physical activity, and self-care. From dozens of podcasts to CNN Health and TIME, the message that well-being is an “inside-out” job is spreading widely!",No,,,,,,United States,Arizona,Phoenix,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/amihungry,Am I Hungry? Mindful Eating Programs and Training,2-10,10,wellness and fitness services,,"The mission of Am I Hungry?® Mindful Eating Programs and Training is to help individuals everywhere eat mindfully and live vibrantly. 

The comprehensive Am I Hungry? Mindful Eating Programs guide participants through the process of relearning to trust their instinctive ability to (mostly) eat when they're hungry, stop when they're full, and address their other triggers for eating in more fulfilling ways. The workshops address the three essential aspects of a sustainable healthy lifestyle:

Think: Conscious decision making using the Am I Hungry?® Mindful Eating Cycle™
Nourish: Nutrition from a non-restrictive, all-foods-fit perspective
Live: Physical activity that is enjoyable and can be integrated into daily life 

Am I Hungry? Mindful Eating Programs are appropriate for individuals who struggle with mindless and emotional eating, yo-yo dieting, diabetes, bariatric surgery, and binge eating. Workshops are available through licensed facilitators, health insurance companies, corporate and worksite wellness programs, medical clinics, hospitals, private coaching and therapy, and other community settings, as well as digital programs and tools.

Am I Hungry? also offers facilitator, coach, and therapist training and licensing for health professionals and other qualified individuals who wish to incorporate mindful eating and intuitive eating into their clinical practice, community, and/or corporate wellness program. 

Founder Michelle May, M.D., award winning author of the Eat What You Love, Love What You Eat book series, is a motivational wellness keynote speaker.",http://amihungry.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/am-i-hungry-mindful-eating-workshops-and-facilitator-training,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,100000-500000,,,amihungry.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
