Ann,"Friedman, Ph.D",Owner,Mindful Being,"Psychologist, Certified Mindfulness Facilitator | Individual & Group Classes, School & Corporate Presentations","I founded Mindful Being Houston, a mindfulness studio in Houston, in 2015. Our certified mindfulness instructors provide warm and inviting group classes for individuals, parents, children, and teens. We offer mindfulness for Houston special events, seminars, workshops, and presentations to corporations, schools, churches, and community groups.

Our goal is to teach people the practice of mindfulness and help them:
Reduce stress
Create a sense of well being
Improve ability to focus and pay attention
Boost immune system functioning
Decrease anxiety, depression, and physical pain
Change the structure and functioning of the brain, including calming areas of emotional reactivity and increasing gray matter in areas of impulse control, judgment, memory, and learning.

Mindfulness meditation changed my life. As a young person, my anxiety increased to a level that caused me suffering. At the time, I was a psychologist who helped others with anxiety, among other issues, but I did not have a personal practice to calm myself. In 2007, I plunged into my first 7-day silent mindfulness retreat.

At the retreat, I learned to watch my own mind for long periods of time. Through this mindful exercise, I saw clearly how the chatter rarely ceased. Much of it was repetitive. I noticed my frustration with people and events that I could not control, as well as regular criticisms of myself and others. I needed to learn how to quiet my mind, find acceptance, and become more compassionate with myself and others through a non-judgmental approach to the present moment. Now, I share this experience with others through mindfulness in Houston.

My credentials:
Certification in Mindfulness Facilitation from the Mindful Awareness Research Center (MARC) of the Semel Institute of Neuroscience and Behavioral Medicine at UCLA
University of Houston - Ph. D, Counseling Psychology
University of Houston - Doctor of Law - JD
The University of Texas Health Science Center at Houston (UTHealth) - Residency, Clinical, Counseling and Applied Psychology
Baylor College of Medicine - Post-Doctoral Fellowship in Clinical Neuropsychology",No,,,,,,United States,Texas,Houston,owner,"education, consulting",https://www.linkedin.com/in/ann-friedman-ph-d-0b9027148,Mindful Being,2-10,7,wellness and fitness services,,"Mindfulness Studio in Houston, Texas. Certified Mindfulness instructors providing group classes for individuals, parents, children, and teens. Offering presentations to corporations, schools, churches, and community groups.",http://www.mindfulbeinghouston.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/mindful-being,SELF_OWNED,0,100000-500000,,,mindfulbeinghouston.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
