Sue,McKinney,Chief Executive Officer | Founder,Altin Biosciences,CEO Altin Biosciences: A Patented Paradigm Shift in Uterine Fibroid Drug Development | Women’s Health Advocates,"I have been a serial entrepreneur from age 12 when I wrote my first business plan, secured friends & family funding, for a business I sold at age 15 for 4X profit. Took the cash and got on a plane to Europe.

Fast forward from a career in law to a patented, non-hormonal uterine fibroid drug candidate - a paradigm shift in fibroid treatment set to capture the market in a $42B problem. At Altin I lead a team of seasoned drug R&D executives with a proven track record of taking products from the lab to market. This is not a team learning on the job; it is the team that defined the field, now developing our own superior solution. Our drug candidate meets patients' and doctors' preference for an oral capsule - easy to take, easy to tolerate, preserves fertility and the uterus

I moved to Vietnam in 1994 where I sourced and developed high-quality exports for Costco, etc. Supporting the dynamic economic and social growth of Vietnam has been a privilege while contributing to a rise in per capital GDP from $225 to $4,717

My 2007 pivot to biotech arose after meeting Doctor Nguyen Thi Ngoc Tram, an internationally award-winning pharmacologist. She developed the medicinal herb Crila with >30 years of research. I reformulated Crila to meet US regulatory standards for Prostate, Menopause and Uterine Health; then sponsored North American studies to further validate Crila's benefits for menopause/prostate health. 

I was introduced to the FDA's Botanical Drug Guidance whereby a plant-based product can receive FDA drug approval. Research at UIC with Drs. Richard Van Breeman and Tristesse Burton confirmed the Crila cultivar is non-estrogenic; presented at NAMS, Publication @Menopause. 

My hypothesis for a novel non-hormonal uterine fibroid drug was tested by KOL Dr. Ayman Al-Hendy @University of Chicago. The Black Women's Health Imperative facilitated ""Directed Donations"" from my supporters to fund pre-clinical testing utilizing human uterine fibroid cells. My hypothesis proved successful resulting in a Composition of Matter patent I share with Adam Payne, CEO Ultra Botanica. 

