My work includes leading formulation strategy, directing scientific teams, and shaping clinical frameworks that integrate pharmacology, diagnostics, and systems-based care. I’ve served as faculty and curriculum developer for organizations including SSRP, A4M, Biote, and Longevitydocs, and I regularly speak at clinical conferences focused on the applied practice of longevity medicine.

I’ve worked with thousands of medical practitioners worldwide—from providers just entering longevity medicine to established practices expanding across multiple locations. That experience includes thousands of 1-on-1 clinical consultations and insight into hundreds of thousands of prescriptions, providing a practical, ground-level view of what works—and what breaks—when longevity medicine meets real practice constraints.

