Mark,Stockhowe,CEO,Vigilant Diagnostics LLC,CEO @ Vigilant Diagnostics & Founder of M.W. Stockhowe & Associates | Helping innovation-driven founders escape the Swirl and scale | Creator of the IDEA System,"If you're an innovation-driven founder whose vision is outpacing your team's ability to execute, you've hit ""the Swirl."" I built the IDEA System to get founders out of it.Every great company begins with a spark: a founder who sees something no one else sees and builds it into something real. But at some point, the thing that made you successful starts working against you. The vision outpaces the organization. Urgency crowds out clarity. And your calendar tells a hard truth: you've become the bottleneck.I call that state ""Swirl."" And after 30 years of working inside and alongside innovation-driven companies, from early-stage startups to growth-stage organizations scaling past 150 people, I built a system to solve it.I also lead one today. As CEO of Vigilant Diagnostics, I use the IDEA System every week to keep a Stage 1 medtech company moving on its vision without letting the Swirl take over. The framework isn't theory. It's how I operate.The Innovation-Driven Execution Accelerator™ (IDEA System) is a four-pillar operating architecture built around Purpose, Plan, Progress, and People. It doesn't ask visionary founders to become operators. It gives them the rhythm, structure, and role clarity to build a company that can execute their vision, without everything running through them.Every engagement starts with the 90-Day Clarity Sprint: One Goal, One Meeting, One Scoreboard. It's a focused trial that proves rhythm creates results before you commit to anything bigger.I literally wrote the book on how to do it:&nbsp;From Swirl to Scale: Turn Your Vision Into Repeatable ResultsIf you're a founder of an innovation-driven company and you're feeling the pull between where you're trying to go and what your team can reliably deliver, let's talk. That gap has a name, and 