Ken,"Coburn MD, DrPH, FACP",CEO & Medical Director,Health Quality Partners (HQP),"CEO, Health Quality Partners (HQP)","My work focuses on health care system redesign to improve population health outcomes.  This pursuit offers a great opportunity to combine my experience in leading teams of health care providers, public health, quality improvement, health policy, managed care, data analysis, design, and systems thinking.

The team at Health Quality Partners (HQP) has developed a new system of advanced preventive care capable of achieving the Triple Aim by focusing on improving health outcomes and relieving suffering among vulnerable populations.  The key design principles of advanced preventive care are: person-centered, population relevant, robust, reliable, accountable, and anticipatory.

This model has been put to the test and proven effective.  HQP was the only care coordination design out of the 15 different programs rigorously tested in the Medicare Coordinated Care Demonstration that improved health outcomes and lowered Medicare expenditures for higher-risk beneficiaries.  A significant and sustained reduction in all-cause mortality was observed among beneficiaries randomized into the intervention arm.  For 7 years, HQP implemented the same model successfully among higher-risk Medicare Advantage members for Aetna in southeastern Pennsylvania.  Through Replication Consultancy, HQP now supports health care organizations in the U.S. and internationally to adopt and extend this model of care.

Our systems design work and applied R&D is now focused on evolving the model to adapt to continually changing care environments, and understanding factors that impact model effectiveness, scalability and dissemination.  Bringing the benefits of this construct for population health to other vulnerable populations through innovations in collaborative partnerships is our next phase of work.  Learn more at www.hqp.org

Specialties: Systems thinking and design, population health, data analytics and visualizations, chronic care coordination, chronic care management, statistics, program evaluation, multidisciplinary team models",No,,,,,,United States,Pennsylvania,Doylestown,c_suite,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/kencoburn,Health Quality Partners (HQP),11-50,12,hospitals and health care,,"Health Quality Partners (HQP) is a not-for-profit organization that does R&D on new models of health care to enhance the effectiveness of preventive interventions and improve population health.  This approach can lower the overall cost of health care for higher risk populations.  This has already been convincingly demonstrated among higher risk chronically ill older adults.  As tested within the Medicare Coordinated Care Demonstration and with Aetna, HQP’s model of Community-based Advanced Preventive Care, significantly reduced hospitalizations, deaths, and total Part A & B Medicare expenditures.

HQP is now inviting organizations to consider becoming strategic partners and early adopters of our model.  The general concept of preventive care services is not new, but a systematic program that reliably delivers a robust set of such services to higher-risk subgroups resulting in better population health and lower health care costs is a breakthrough innovation.  If your organization appreciates the relative advantage this innovation offers and feels it is compatible with your culture and mission, contact us.  Your organization might be a good candidate to be an early adopter.  We anticipate that in 2022 we'll also invite organizations with whom we collaborate to begin designing a learning network to accelerate applied R&D for population health management - think 'users group'​, but with shared research, analytical, and design capabilities.

With the availability of HQP's new System as a Service (SPERO®), and Replication Consultancy, we can help organizations anywhere in the world implement our proven program for chronically ill older adults on a large scale, as well as embark on new R&D work to innovate programs for other vulnerable populations.  For all of its initiatives, HQP uses a disciplined framework for program design and implementation based on key design principles; person-centered, population-relevant, robust, reliable, accountable, anticipatory.",http://www.hqp.org,https://www.linkedin.com/company/health-quality-partners,NON_PROFIT,0,500000-1000000,,,hqp.org,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
