Manisha,Lad,Founder & Executive Director,The Sensory Pathway center,"Founder | Sensory Pathway Center & Akhil Autism Foundation | Building NESTURE – AI & Gesture-Based Learning for Non-Speaking Autistic Individuals | Neurodevelopment, Innovation & Advocacy","My mantra:
“Each day I will make a difference in someone’s life — and transform myself every moment.”
This belief has guided my life as a mother, leader, advocate, and innovator.

I bring over 16 years of experience in Information Technology, having worked with global organizations such as Siebel Systems and MetLife. In 2001, when our son—now 25 years old—was diagnosed with autism, my career and purpose shifted entirely. I stepped away from a successful IT trajectory to support his development at a time when we were told not to expect progress.

Through persistence, science-based interventions, and a deep trust in his abilities, he has defied every limitation. Today, he is pursuing college education and thriving as a non-speaking communicator, showing the world what is possible when the right support system exists.

This journey became the foundation of my life’s work.
Founder, Akhil Autism Foundation (Nonprofit)

In 2008, I established the Akhil Autism Foundation to bring awareness, education, and global resources to families navigating autism. Over the years, the foundation has grown into a hub for parent empowerment, professional training, and globally accessible neurodevelopmental programs.

🏥 Founder, Sensory Pathway Center (Therapy & Innovation Hub)

I later founded the Sensory Pathway Center, a neuroscience-aligned therapeutic program serving neurodiverse children, teens, and adults.
Our model integrates:
	•	Primitive Reflex Integration
	•	MNRI & QRI
	•	Sensory Regulation & Motor Planning
	•	Interactive Metronome & Smart Ball
	•	RPM & Mind–Body–Communication support
	•	Pre-vocational and community integration pathways
We provide families not only with therapy, but with a roadmap to progress—connecting sensory, motor, cognitive, and emotional development.
🌱 Creator, Neurodiverse Gardeners (Nature-Based Vocational Program)
I lead Neurodiverse Gardeners, a pre-vocational and employment-readiness program using hydroponic microgreens, horticulture, and green-industry activities.
This program builds responsibility, planning, sequencing, and meaningful community participation, offering a dignified pathway toward independence and future employment.
