Phoebe (Thuy),Casey,President & Operating Officer (COO) / Co-Founder,RxWellness Spine & Health,Award-winning President & Operating Officer  / Founder RxWellness LLC and Family of Companies,"I've spent over 30 years building enterprise value — leading large-scale transformations, complex integrations, and growth strategies for some of the world's most recognized organizations. From the Marriott / Starwood integration to Simon & Schuster / Pearson, and across Capital One, Callaway Golf, Pfizer, Johnson & Johnson, and AstraZeneca — my career has been defined by one discipline: building scalable platforms that perform.

Today, as President and Chief Operating Officer of RxWellness Spine & Health, I'm applying that same operating rigor to one of the most compelling platform opportunities in healthcare.

RxWellness is a growing multi-site, multi-region chiropractic, rehabilitation, and medical wellness platform — and a category worth paying attention to. Demand is structural. The shift from reactive, episodic care toward integrated, preventive wellness is not a trend. It is a fundamental reorientation of how patients engage with their health, creating significant white space for scaled operators who can execute.

Most patients enter our platform seeking relief — lower back pain, neck pain, headaches, joint discomfort, or injury recovery. Resolving that pain is the entry point. The platform opportunity lies in what comes next: guiding patients from acute pain care toward long-term wellness — and ultimately, a longer, healthier life. That transition, from reactive treatment to proactive health optimization, is where the real value is created — for patients and for the platform.

Higher patient lifetime value. Stronger retention. A differentiated model that competitors cannot easily replicate.

My focus at RxWellness is building the infrastructure that makes scale possible and sustainable — standardized operating systems, leadership development pipelines, consistent clinical delivery, and the organizational architecture needed to support site growth, strategic partnerships, and M&A integration.
My operating thesis is straightforward: exceptional patient outcomes and strong unit economics are not in tension. When the clinical model is right, the systems are tight, and the teams are developed — financial performance follows. That's not a philosophy. That's a pattern I've seen repeat for three decades.

RxWellness is not simply adding locations. We are building a platform — one with the systems, talent, and strategic clarity to scale with discipline, capture market share in a fragmented space, and deliver durable enterprise value.

