Igor,Bogorad,Co-founder & Director of NGS,Angstrom Innovation,Co-founder & Director of NGS,"I am the co-founder of a new biotech company called Angstrom Innovation. We offer premium NGS sequencing services to our customers.


Previously at Bota Bio, I led a 20-person international team to build a world-class Biofoundry in driving innovations in strain and enzyme engineering for human nutrition, dairy, biopreservatives, and personal care. We developed:
✅ Automated DNA construction with NGS validation in under 2 weeks
✅ High-throughput transformation across diverse microbial hosts
✅ AI-assisted enzyme engineering with site-directed and combinatorial libraries
✅ Adaptive strain evolution to enhance industrial performance

As the technical lead on Bota’s highest-priority project, my team doubled strain performance, securing the company’s largest revenue stream in 2024. Today, Bota Bio is the global leader in nisin production (BioShield™ HG-Nis), with manufacturing in Shandong, China.

At Amyris, I focused on metabolic engineering of trans-β-Farnesene, pioneering a 13C amino acid assay to map metabolic flux. My research uncovered inefficiencies in the oxidative pentose phosphate pathway (oxPPP), leading to strain redesigns that significantly improved sugar yield. Additionally, I modeled metabolic pathways for Rebaudioside M (a natural sweetener), convincing the team to target the pgi/pgm node—a decision that led to dramatic strain improvements. My final project involved engineering a non-natural steroid in S. cerevisiae in collaboration with an international partner.

At UCLA, I secured a $3M grant from ARPA-e REMOTE program as a postdoc to re-engineer E. coli central metabolism, enabling the conversion of methanol into higher-energy alcohols with 100% carbon efficiency—a project inspired by my PhD research.
During my PhD at UCLA, I developed the groundbreaking ""Non-Oxidative Glycolysis"" pathway to prevent carbon loss during sugar metabolism, published in Nature (2013).
Throughout my career, I’ve been fortunate to work with incredible mentors, including Dr. James C. Liao (Academia Sinica President), Dr. Adam Meadows (Amyris, Data Science Director), and Dr. Cheryl Cui (Bota Bio CEO).

