Tony,Schueth,Chairman and Chief Executive Officer,Point-of-Care Partners,"CEO and Chairman of the Board at Point-of-Care Partners, Inc","I am the founder, chairman of the Board and current CEO of Point-of-Care Partners, an employee-owned healthcare management consulting firm, life sciences marketing agency narrowly focused on the electronic health record and health IT Federal and state regulatory research group. We transitioned to being employee-owned in 2023, 20 years after I founded the firm.

I am also chairman of the board and president of Aditus Healthcare Technologies, Inc., a healthcare technolgoy services company.

A 36-year healthcare veteran, I have spent the last 30 years working to provide decision support, communication and other tools at the point-of-care. An expert in heath IT, in general, and one of the foremost experts in automated Medication Management, I have accumulated experience in healthcare IT and digital health, and an extensive network of contacts. 

Both POCP and Aditus are committed to helping lead the growth of healthcare, and giving back. In addiiton to being the leader of each company, I serve the industry as well. I am the chair of the  designated subcommittee of the NCPDP Foundation and participate on several HL7 workgroups including Pharmacy and EHR. After hosting three highly successful fundraisers for the Lewy Body Dementia Association, I served on its board as a Vice President.

An accomplished public speaker, I also serve as editor-in-chief of POCP's newsletter, HIT Perspectives; publisher of four of its regulatory reports/services; a blogger and a former columnist for HealthTech Zone. Here is a link to POCP's content: www.pocp.com (Insights). 

POCP's clients are a “who’s who” of payers (health plans, employers and PBMs), life sciences companies, provider organizations, technology companies, health information exchanges, federal and state government agencies and other healthcare organizations. Here is more info about the firm: http://goo.gl/4zHT7G. Aditus's clients are payers, providers and life sciences companies.

