Edward,Filardo,Co-Founder and Chief Scientific Officer,"Starling Biosciences, Inc.","Mechanistic Oncology & GPCR Strategy | Advancing High-Impact Science into Fundable, Partner-Ready Programs","Director-level oncology and inflammation pharmacology leader with over 25 years of experience translating GPCR biology into IND-enabled and clinical-stage therapeutics. My work spans target identification, mechanistic pharmacology, translational strategy, and early development, with a consistent focus on advancing scientifically compelling programs into therapies that can reach patients. As CSO and co-founder of Starling Biosciences, I have led development of GPCR-targeted therapeutics, including both modulator and targeted protein degrader approaches. Previously, as Director of Oncology and Inflammation at Cytonus Therapeutics, I helped advance a precision cell-based delivery platform across oncology and inflammatory disease, contributing to &gt;$5M in non-dilutive funding support through DoD, NIH, and CIRM programs. Across these roles, a recurring theme has been working at the interface of strong biology and translational execution—where many early-stage programs struggle to define a credible path toward funding, partnership, or clinical advancement. In parallel, I work with biotech and academic teams to sharpen mechanism-driven development strategy, translational positioning, and non-dilutive funding readiness for high-risk/high-impact oncology and platform biotechnology programs. This has included supporting NIH, DoD, ARPA-H, and SBIR proposal development, shaping translational plans, defining milestone architecture, and helping teams identify the key experiments needed to unlock funding and external engagement. I have also served on NIH/NCI SBIR review panels evaluating translational oncology and platform biotechnology proposals, providing additional perspective into how scientifically ambitious programs are assessed for impact, feasibility, and translational readiness. 