Christopher,Thanos,Chairman and CEO,XDemics Corporation,"Chairman and CEO, XDemics Corporation","Over 30 years of R&amp;D experience, including 26 years in the biotechnology industry building significant value for investors.  Named inventor on 35 issued and multiple pending patent applications, and a first author of multiple peer-reviewed articles in top tier scientific journals.   Named one of the top 25 CEOs in biotech by Healthcare Technology Report in 2022.Chairman and CEO of XDemics Corporation, a Caltech spinout fundamentally improving the way cells are grown.  XDemics is developing the High-Density Cell Respiration (HDCR™) platform to overcome the oxygen delivery and shear stress limitations of conventional cell culture systems, generating therapeutic cells and viruses with&nbsp;improved potency and quality at&nbsp;10-100X higher cell densities.   $1.55B estimated TAM.Co-Founder of Voro Therapeutics, developing a category-defining tumor-activated biologics platform.  Assembled the founding team at Actym Therapeutics, raised initial capital ($66M),  and established therapeutic platform (multiple issued US patents).  Nominated and initiated development of Actym's first clinical candidate, ACTM-838 (co-inventor), currently in Phase 1 development stage.  Contributed to the FDA approval of Halozyme's ENHANZE delivery platform, embedded in 10 commercial products at a company valued at ~$7.7B (over 1M patients treated).Co-invented core platform technology at Sutro Biopharma now underpinning four ADCs in development and two vaccine candidates in Phase 3 at Vaxcyte (~$8B market cap).  Co-inventor of platform and two programs at Catalyst Biosciences acquired by Pfizer and Vertex, generating over $100M in combined cash milestones.•  Significant entrepreneurial and executive leadership experience in the biotechnology industry•  Design, engineering of production technologies, development of cell therapies, ADC's, enzymes•  Comprehensive understanding of pipeline flow, from lead optimization to IND, to clinical POC•  Established skills in fundraising, strategy, due diligence, portfolio management•  First author publications in high impact factor journals such as Science, PNAS, JACS•  Effectively managed large teams•  Invited speaker, workshop leader, conference chair at several international meetings",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,Belvedere Tiburon,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/christopher-thanos-35972a37,XDemics Corporation,2-10,19,biotechnology research,,"XDemics, a Caltech spinout, is fundamentally improving the way cells are grown. We’ve addressed a primary bottleneck—the basic inability to efficiently transfer oxygen in media during cell growth.

Our high-density cell respiration (HDCR) technology enables mammalian cells to grow at 20- to 100-fold higher densities—whether in a Petri dish or a large-scale bioreactor. As a result, scientists and manufacturers can produce more high-quality, viable cells in far less space and time, dramatically slashing R&D and manufacturing costs.

From the lab bench to industrial-scale production, HDCR is transformative. One Expansify™ Petri dish replaces 25 traditional polystyrene dishes, vastly accelerating biomedical innovation while cutting costs. With predictable process scale-up, our Profusion-Midi™ 5L and Profusion-Max™ 50L bioreactors can respectively generate up to 1–10 trillion cells, eliminating the need for massive, complicated 200–2000L stirred-tank vessels.

HDCR systems deliver high-quality cell and gene therapies more efficiently, reducing the overall cost of these advanced medicines by up to 80%, achieving cost parity with biologics and making these life-changing treatments more accessible worldwide.

Our laboratory facilities are located on the beautiful campus of the world-famous Buck Institute in Marin County, California.",https://xdemics.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/xdemics-corporation,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,1000000-5000000,5543624,UNDISCLOSED,xdemics.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
