Rajee,Hari,Founder & CEO,Protean Med Inc.,"Founder & CEO @ Protean Med | Placing Physicians, NPs, PAs & CRNAs Nationwide | Host, ProteanPulse Podcast | Author, Monday Morning Coffee ☕","I didn't start out in healthcare staffing. I started in a lab.

After earning my Master's in Biochemistry and spending years in pharmaceutical research at Genentech and Lexicon, I pivoted into business — completing my Executive MBA at Texas A&M and taking on operations leadership at BizTech Solutions. It was a winding path. But every step taught me something about what it truly means to find the right fit — the right role, the right environment, the right challenge.

That insight is what led me to found Protean Med in 2020, right in the middle of a global pandemic that exposed just how fragile healthcare staffing really was.

At Protean Med, we connect Physicians, Nurse Practitioners, Physician Assistants, and CRNAs with locum, permanent, and locum-to-perm opportunities across the country. We work with clinicians at every stage — from new graduates figuring out their first role, to experienced providers ready for a change — and with healthcare facilities that need reliable, high-quality coverage fast.

What makes us different? We don't just fill slots. We listen. We match on values, lifestyle, and long-term fit — not just credentials and availability.

Beyond recruiting, I host ProteanPulse — a podcast where I sit down with physicians, specialists, and healthcare leaders to talk about the real challenges and rewards of practicing medicine today. It keeps me connected to the clinicians I serve, and reminds me every week why this work matters.

Every Monday I also write Monday Morning Coffee — a short, honest read about entrepreneurship, intentional living, healthcare, and the messy, meaningful journey of building something from scratch. Topics range from the productivity of rest and choosing intention over momentum, to what healthcare staffing has taught me about people and purpose. If any of that resonates, follow along on LinkedIn or at www.proteanmed.com.

