Craig,Lindell,Co-Founder,Prehab,I help people get out of pain and prevent injuries by expanding global access to physical therapy with [P]rehab,"Craig Lindell, PT, DPT, CSCSCo-Founder of [P]rehab &amp; [P]rehab Physical TherapyIronman &amp; Ultramarathon AthleteI believe physical therapy has an access problem. Our purpose at [P]rehab is to redefine it.Only 10% of people who could benefit from physical therapy ever actually get to a physical therapist. Worse, most people only encounter PT after something breaks. And when they do, they spend about 1 hour a week with their clinician. That's only 0.6% of their entire week. The other 99.4%? They're on their own.I've spent the last decade building solutions for every side of that equation.For the public: We've built a community of 2.5M+ followers and 100K+ users across 180+ countries on the #1 rated physical therapy app to educate people on the value of proactive movement. We want to change the conversation from ""I need PT because I'm hurt"" to ""I do prehab so I don't get hurt.""For clinicians: We built [P]rehab Professional, a clinical HEP platform used by 6,000+ PTs, ATCs, and movement professionals across 1,000+ clinics &amp; athletic departments, 50+ professional sports organizations, and 30+ DPT &amp; MSAT programs. 50,000+ patients go through the platform every month. Because the quality of care shouldn't drop the moment a patient walks out your door.For patients: We opened [P]rehab Physical Therapy in Los Angeles, concierge, one-on-one, no shortcuts. Because sometimes you need a clinician in the room, not just a phone or a piece of paper to refer to.It all started when I co-founded The [P]rehab Guys in a PT school basement in 2016. No VC, no playbook. Just a belief that physical therapy is too important to be this hard to access.We're building a future where people can prevent injuries, get out of pain, and get connected with clinicians more easily - because every other aspect of our life is already easier with technology. PT shouldn't be the exception.My family, coffee, cars, cooking, training, hiking, and golfing consume the other time that I have.I write here to share my story &amp; mentor others about clinical decision-making, building a health tech company as a clinician, and why the public perception of PT is still broken. If any of that resonates - let's connect.",No,,,,,,United States,Oregon Metropolitan Area,Portland,founder,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/craig-lindell-prehab,Prehab,11-50,17,wellness and fitness services,,"A new era of [P]rehab is here! 

