My mission is to expand access to effective, stigma-free addiction support through in-person and online programs, enabling more individuals and families to experience the dignity and positive change they deserve. At ARS, my team and I help people change by exploring the connections between their actions, beliefs, and emotions in a safe collaborative environment that guides people to a personalized plan for change. We create space for individuals to take meaningful steps toward recovery through support and collaboration with healthcare professionals.


SERVICES:
 
At ARS, our team of skilled addiction professionals provides two key service lines:
 
✅ Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP): Our traditional, insurance-reimbursed treatment program offers structured, evidence-based care to those in the Southern NH, ME, and Northern MA areas through both in-person at our office in Greenland, NH, and via telehealth services.
 
✅ Online Curriculum & Coaching: This flexible, accessible program brings the skills and insights of intensive outpatient treatment directly into clients' homes, making it perfect for those who don’t have time for a traditional rehab program or who want to maintain privacy during their recovery. This service includes personalized coaching and family education to support sustainable recovery. Anyone can find out more about this program by using this calendar link: https://calendly.com/john-iudice

I can also provide training and supervision on evidence-based practices, such as Motivational Interviewing and Cognitive Behavioral Therapy, to other organizations. I am also an adjunct faculty member at the University of New Hampshire's Master of Social Work program, where I teach courses on addiction treatment and counseling practices. Outside of work, I reside in the Seacoast area with my wife and three children.


