Greg,Kunst,Chief Executive Officer and Board Member,Valitor,Biotech CEO & Board Chairman | Building What Doesn’t Yet Exist in Life Sciences & Medicine | EY Entrepreneur of the Year,"I've spent 25 years building things that didn't yet exist.Not incrementally better versions of what came before — genuinely first-in-kind treatments, platforms, and companies that address diseases millions of people live with and that the world has largely stopped trying to solve. Today I serve as CEO and Board Member of&nbsp;Valitor, a Berkeley-based biotechnology company engineering the next generation of long-acting ophthalmic medicines. Our platform uses multivalent biopolymer conjugation technology to take proven bioactive molecules and dramatically extend their therapeutic durability — starting with a long-acting VEGF inhibitor designed to reliably deliver six months or more of efficacy from a single dose. For the millions of patients with wet AMD and other retinal diseases who require injections every 8–12 weeks indefinitely, that's not an incremental improvement — it's a fundamental change in what treatment looks like. Backed by Morningside Ventures and led by a seasoned team of biotech executives, engineers, and drug developers, Valitor is using best-in-class science to solve one of the most persistent unmet needs in ophthalmology. I joined because the platform is real, the team is exceptional, and the mission is exactly the kind of thing I've spent my career building toward.My career has been built on three values I hold deeply:&nbsp;Conviction, because biotech is hard and near-death experiences are part of every company's story.&nbsp;Responsibility, because every dollar of capital and every patient who needs a treatment is sacred.&nbsp;Pioneering, because incremental is not interesting — the goal is always the step-change that changes millions of lives.I also serve as Board Chairman of Biomimetix, alongside independent board seats at Pr3vent, Feliqs, and SIME Diagnostics. My work is focused on helping life sciences companies navigate the moments that matter most.I'm particularly interested in serving as an independent board director and board chairman for companies in ophthalmology, neurosciences, immunology, oncology, cell and gene therapy, biologics, and broader life sciences — at any stage from Series A through pre-commercialization. I'm also open to venture partner relationships and strategic advisory engagements where I can put 25 years of hard-won operating experience to work.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Washington,Seattle,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/gregkunst,Valitor,2-10,20,biotechnology research,,"Valitor, Inc. is a biotechnology company founded to develop advanced, protein-based drugs. Using our core technology, we can modify existing biological therapies to achieve substantial control over their pharmacological properties. Our mission is to develop a new generation of biologic therapies that will reduce the costs associated with effective treatment of these diseases. We also aim to improve the patients’ quality of life by reducing the required frequency of therapeutic administration. We have initiated a pipeline of drug products that will be used to treat a variety of diseases currently imposing a significant financial burden on the nation’s healthcare system.

