Dr. Jonathon,"Harrison, PharmD, ACE",President and CEO,Wellyfe,"Founder & CEO @ Wellyfe | helping hospitals, FQHCs & employers save up to 60% on pharmacy benefits | 340B advocate","I build pharmacy benefits that put communities—not middlemen—first.

I’m the Founder & CEO of Wellyfe, a transparent PBM alternative built for hospitals, FQHCs, and employer groups. We help organizations save up to 60% on pharmacy benefits, keep care local by empowering independent pharmacies, and turn pharmacy from a cost center into a community asset. No rebate games. No black boxes. Just clear pricing, clinical guardrails, and results your CFO can defend.

But before I ever started building PBMs, I fell in love with pharmacy because of one patient.

When I was a high school research intern at the Cleveland Clinic, I was working on the behavioral health floor when a patient had a complete mental breakdown—he went catatonic. For two weeks, he didn’t speak or move.

Then one day, a clinical pharmacist adjusted his medication regimen. Within days, that same man was sitting upright, talking, and later—reunited with his family of five.

That moment changed everything for me.

I saw what pharmacy could do when it was personal, clinical, and human.

That’s what drives me still.

At Wellyfe, we’re reimagining pharmacy benefits with that same purpose: helping people get their lives back—not just their prescriptions filled.

What we do at Wellyfe

Direct Pharmacy Care (PBM alternative): Transparent pricing, member-first design, and local network enablement.

340B optimization: Expand capture, protect audits, and grow mission revenue.
PA reduction & formulary management: Eliminate low-value barriers while preserving clinical safety.
Commercialization for employers: Bring local self-funded employer plans to life.

Data & accountability: Real-time analytics, CFO-grade reporting, and measurable outcomes.
Outside of work

You’ll find me hiking, fishing, chasing after my three kids and six dogs, and trading spreadsheets for mountain trails. Those miles on the trail remind me a lot of this work—steady, uphill, but worth every step.

Want to rebuild pharmacy benefits where you live and work?

🔗 wellyferx.com

