Katie,Quine,Registered Nurse Coordinator,Connecticut Hospice,"Hospice & Healthcare Leader | Founder, Leaders on Edge™ | I rebuild teams from the culture up — fully compliant AND fully human","I’m the Founder of Leaders on Edge™, a leadership development platform for building grounded, emotionally intelligent leaders in high-stakes environments.

My background is in hospice — as an executive, an RN, and a healthcare operator. I’ve led clinical teams, navigated regulatory complexity I once genuinely mistook for industry slang, managed growth, and built culture in places where the stakes are real and the margin for error is razor-thin.

Most of what I know about leadership, I learned the way everyone actually does: by getting some of it wrong first, and being lucky enough to have people who taught me instead of letting me drown.

Here’s what it all taught me:

Technical skill sustains operations.
Leadership climate sustains people.
You need both. Most organizations pour everything into the first and assume the second will sort itself out. It doesn’t — and that gap is where good people quietly burn out and leave.

Through Leaders on Edge™, I help healthcare and mission-driven leaders:

• Strengthen leadership capacity
• Build psychologically safe, high-accountability cultures
• Prevent burnout without lowering the bar
• Navigate growth with clarity and steadiness
• Lead without sacrificing integrity

Underneath all of it is a conviction I can’t shake: you can be fully compliant and fully human at the same time. I’ve spent a career proving it — and calling out the false choice every time someone insists it can’t be done.

And if I’m honest about what lights me up most: it’s the hands-on work. Walking into a struggling organization and taking it apart from the inside out — finding what’s actually broken underneath what looks broken, and rebuilding it from the culture up. That’s the work I believe in most, and the work I’ll always make room for.

Because here’s what I keep coming back to: leadership isn’t about control. It’s about the environment you create.

The way you lead at work follows people home.
—
Hospice & Healthcare Leader | Executive Coach | Founder, Leaders on Edge™
Where Grounded Leadership Meets Courageous Growth™",No,,,,,,United States,Connecticut,New Milford,founder,medical_health,https://www.linkedin.com/in/leadersonedge,Connecticut Hospice,201-500,132,hospitals and health care,,"The Connecticut Hospice provides comprehensive and compassionate hospice, palliative and other supportive care management services.  Whether at home, assisted living center, skilled nursing facility, or at our inpatient waterfront hospital, we are here to guide you.",https://hospice.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-connecticut-hospice-inc,NON_PROFIT,0,5000000-10000000,,,hospice.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
