Lew,Zeidner,Chief Executive Officer,EOSIS,"CEO EOSIS (formerly Meridian Behavioral Health, LLC)","Virtually all organizations are flush with good ideas; potential strategic and tactical changes that could make a real difference for customers, co-workers and shareholders.  Very few organizations are effective at translating good ideas to operational or financial realities.

The challenge is rarely motivation, intelligence or intention on the part of executives or staff.  The core obstacle is most often in defining the detailed process changes needed to operationalize the ideas.  
•	How does technology need to change?  
•	How does every element of workflow impacted need to change?  
•	What are the challenges and are they able to be overcome on a reasonable timeline and budget.  
•	Who are the likely saboteurs and what will it take to engage them?
•	What are the unintended negative consequences of these changes to other parts of the customer experience or processes?

What I do is make good ideas come alive in organizations!

Some mis-label this process as project management; it is not.  Any strategic organizational change requires management of a multitude of projects, but they do not succeed or fail simply based on how the projects are managed.  Success requires an understanding and leadership plan for changing core organizational patterns that create obstacles to growth.

If you are ready to see your organization’s strategy become a reality, let’s talk.",Yes,,,,,,United States,,Greater Minneapolis-st. Paul Area,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/lewzeidnerceo,EOSIS,501-1000,446,mental health care,,"EOSIS is a network of behavioral health centers headquartered in New Brighton, Minnesota. Operating on the belief that everyone deserves quality care, EOSIS employs a dedicated team of professionals aligned around a common goal, tied together by a shared therapeutic approach and uniformly, passionately committed to driving better life outcomes. EOSIS addresses diverse populations and facilitates personalized treatment, providing care outcomes that improve the lives of the patients, families and communities we serve. Because we believe everyone deserves a chance to experience a new dawn.",http://www.eosisrecovery.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/eosisrecovery,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,10000000-25000000,,PRIVATE_EQUITY_ROUND,www.meridianprograms.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
