ation with Judah Folkman at Boston Children's Hospital, he led the thalidomide program contributing to its approval in multiple myeloma and sold today by BMS.  He also co-founded MaxCyte with Doug Doerfler and John Holaday to commercialize electroporation technology, a spinout of EntreMed.  MaxCyte is now a clinical-stage company enabling next-generation cell-based therapeutics.In collaboration with IBM Life Sciences and John Wiley &amp; Sons to included clients such as Fujitsu, Itochu, and J&amp;J, he founded Labbook.com, bioinformatics platform company focused on integrating and sharing targeted datasets to accelerate translational research and drug development.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Maryland,Rockville,c_suite,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/shawngreen,MTEC | Medical Technology Enterprise Consortium,11-50,19,biotechnology research,,"MTEC is a biomedical technology consortium collaborating with multiple government agencies under a 10-year renewable Other Transaction Agreement (OTA) with the U.S. Army Medical Research and Materiel Command (USAMRMC).

