Thomas,Treynor,Co-Founder and CEO,"R2DIO, The Data Improvement Company","Co-founder and CEO, R2DIO","More data helps, but better data helps more! I help R&amp;D and Manufacturing teams scale faster, cheaper and with more predictability by making their data fit-for-use and AI-ready.Whether you're a lab scientist analyzing a curated table or a data scientist feeding batch records to an AI agent, you can't generate signals from noise. The power of LLMs emerge from grafting the collective wisdom of The Web onto a small prompt, while the power of AlphaFold emerges from combining two large databases benefitting from decades of investment into measurement precision and accuracy. The challenge for today's scientists and engineers is that most of the data they rely on for discovery, process development and optimization at scale is relatively sparse, under-replicated and incompletely annotated. Their data is also proprietary, so they can’t rely on the wisdom of the crowd to generate insights only their team could possibly know. Ultimately their insights are only as good as their data.When I was an independent scientific and statistical consultant, I observed time and again how conventional software architectures (e.g., ELNs and LIMS) were perpetuating the epidemic of low data quality instead of curing it. So I co-founded R2DIO to improve the&nbsp;completeness, reproducibility and availability of R&amp;D and QC data on a global scale. Our customers in biotech, pharma, agtech, chemicals and foodtech use the speed and flexibility of R2DIO's Process Data Fabric to make even their most integration-resistant measurements and metadata easily queried (FAIR) and richly contextualized as a complete and continuously improvable knowledge graph.Since 2021 I've been teaching a one-month course on R&amp;D Quality Management in the Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at UC Berkeley. I was also the chair of SynBioBeta's Working Group on R&amp;D Performance Improvement.Please visit https://r2dio.regfox.com/how-to-do-in-spec-r-and-d to learn about my next Workshop on Data Quality. (""10/10. This is a workshop that all scientists should be taking prior to researching."")",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,Berkeley,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/ttreynor,"R2DIO, The Data Improvement Company",2-10,5,biotechnology research,,"Scaling new and improved processes is already hard enough. Don't let bad data make it harder! R2DIO’s software and services address the epidemic of poor data quality at both of its roots: incompleteness and irreproducibility.

