Daniel F.,"Kelly, MD",Director & Founder,Pacific Neuroscience Institute (PNI),"Neurosurgeon | Director & Founder, Pacific Neuroscience Institute | Minimally Invasive Brain, Skull Base & Pituitary Tumor Surgery | Founder & CEO, Psychedelic Science Institute","Dr. Kelly, a board certified neurosurgeon, is Director and one of the Founders of Pacific Neuroscience Institute, a multispecialty group of over 40 physicians and clinician scientists working across 10 Centers of Excellence. He directs the Pacific Brain Tumor and Pituitary Disorders Centers at Providence Saint John’s Health Center, is Professor of Neurosurgery at Saint John's Cancer Institute and on the PNI Foundation board. He is also CEO of the newly formed Psychedelic Science Institute. 

In practice for over 30 years, he is considered a world leader in advancing minimally invasive keyhole and endoscopic approaches for brain, skull base and pituitary tumors. He has one of the largest series in endonasal transsphenoidal surgery with over 2500 procedures performed and over 2000 craniotomies for brain and skull base tumors. 

He is a recipient of the Southern California Super Doctors distinction for 17 years (2007-2024), has over 150 peer-reviewed publications and 40 book chapters, mostly focused on minimally invasive surgical techniques, surgical outcomes and complication avoidance. He has a long-standing commitment to medical education, neurosurgery fellowship training and patient education, and lectures frequently at national and international meetings. 

Over the last 7 years, he has increasingly focused his attention on advancing novel mental health care solutions. He was the creative force behind the Pacific Brain Health Center in 2018, aimed at preventing and reversing dementia. 

In 2019, he launched the Pacific Treatment & Research in Psychedelics (TRIP) Center (led by Dr. Keith Heinzerling), focused on studying the use of psychedelic medicines as neuroplastogens and the exploration of how psychedelic-assisted therapy can improve mood, brain health and quality of life. 

In July 2025, the PNI TRIP Center transitioned into the independent Psychedelic Science Institute with Dr. Kelly as CEO along with 4 other cofounders Dr. Keith Heinzerling, Brooke Balliett, LMFT, Micah Linton, PsyD, and Gregory Kearns, MHA. 

Dr. Kelly is a graduate of Claremont McKenna College (1982), Georgetown University School of Medicine (1986) and completed neurosurgical training at George Washington University (1993). He was Professor of Neurosurgery and Vice-Chief of UCLA Division of Neurosurgery until 2007 then joined Saint John’s Health Center, where he served on the Board of Directors from 2014-2021 and was Chief of Neurosurgery from 2010-2021. In 2021 he completed the CIIS Certificate in Psychedelic-Assisted Therapies and Research training program.",No,,,,,,United States,California,Santa Monica,founder,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/daniel-f-kelly-md-190b84122,Pacific Neuroscience Institute (PNI),51-200,107,hospitals and health care,,"The Pacific Neuroscience Institute (PNI) is devoted to the care of patients with a wide spectrum of neurological and cranial disorders including: brain tumors, skull base tumors and pituitary tumors; spine health; stroke and related neurovascular diseases; adult hydrocephalus; vision and hearing disorders; facial pain and paralysis syndromes; movement disorders as well as sinonasal tumors and related disorders. Additionally our brain health team cares for a wide spectrum of behavioral and cognitive disorder as well as autoimmune and neuroinflammatory disease such as Multiple Sclerosis.

PNI encompasses 11 Centers of Excellence which provide comprehensive management of these disorders and conditions:  
-	Pacific Brain Health Center
-	Pacific Brain Tumor Center
-	Pacific Pituitary Disorders Center
-	Pacific Stroke Center
-	Pacific Adult Hydrocephalus Center
-	Pacific Facial Pain Center
-	Pacific Movement Disorders Center
-	Pacific Eye, Ear & Skull Base Center
-	Pacific Spine Health Center
-	Pacific Neuroscience Research Center
-       Pacific Treatment & Research in Psychedelics

PNI has 35 physician specialists across multiple disciplines. PNI Medical Group & Affiliate specialities include:
Neurosurgery, neuro-oncology, neurology, neuro-ophthalmology, interventional neuroradiology, radiation oncology, endocrinology, ENT (otolaryngology - head & neck surgery), neuro-anesthesia, neuropathology, psychiatry, clinical psychology, and addiction medicine. 

PNI is focused on providing state-of-the-art care with a focus on minimally invasive surgical and interventional techniques. In collaboration with the Saint John's Cancer Institute, PNI is also focused on translational research and clinical trials as well as fellowship education and continuing medical education.",http://PacificNeuro.org,https://www.linkedin.com/company/pacific-neuroscience-institute-pni,NON_PROFIT,0,5000000-10000000,,,pacificneuroscienceinstitute.org,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
Michael,"Farrell DC, MBA, CSSBB",Chief Executive Officer,St. Croix Regional Family Health Center,"Strategic CEO @SCRFHC | Championing health access| Driving Operational Efficiency, value and expansion","As the CEO of St. Criox Regional Family Health Center, I lead the strategic direction and daily operations of an extensive healthcare network dedicated to serving rural communities in Maine. With over ten years of experience in the healthcare industry, I previously held roles such as COO and Director of Rehabilitation Services at KVHC and Doctor of Chiropractic at Penobscot Community Health Care. My academic background includes an MBA in Health/Health Care Administration/Management from Husson University and a Doctor of Chiropractic degree from Logan University, complemented by certifications in acupuncture and active release techniques. Proficient in professional communication, problem-solving, and business management, my commitment lies in enhancing healthcare quality and accessibility for underserved populations, aligning closely with the mission, vision, and values of St. Criox Regional Family Health Center.",No,,,,,,United States,Maine,Lincoln,c_suite,"master_operations, c_suite",https://www.linkedin.com/in/michael-farrell-dc-mba-cssbb-772739197,St. Croix Regional Family Health Center,11-50,26,hospitals and health care,,"The St. Croix Regional Family Health Center (SCRFHC) is a Federally Qualified Community Health Center (FQHC). We are a private, nonprofit organization, which has been providing health care since 1991. No one will be denied access to services due to an inability to pay. We offer discounts based on family size and income.

The Health Center was founded in 1991 after a group of concerned citizens met in the kitchen of one of the present Board members to seek a resolution to the virtually complete absence of primary care services in Northern Washington County.

The original health center was located in rented space on the main street and had one medical provider, a nurse, and a receptionist. The volume of patients seeking care soon required expansion, however, and funds were eventually raised to build a new health center at the current location on Mill Street in 1998. There were only enough funds to complete the top floor of the two-story building at that time, but the first floor space has been worked on over the past couple of years, and will be completed this year. We were able to add Mental Health and Substance Abuse services in 1993. 

We are fortunate to have an extremely dedicated and able Board of Directors, several of whom have remained on the Board since the health center's inception. They all reside in the community, many are health center patients, and their insight and judgment has ensured that the health center continues to grow at a steady and fiscally responsible rate.",http://scrfhc.org,https://www.linkedin.com/company/st-croix-regional-family-health-center,NON_PROFIT,0,1000000-5000000,,,scrfhc.org,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
