"Walter ""Buzz""",Stewart,CEO,Medcurio,40 Years Solving Healthcare’s Hardest Translation Problems | CEO | Real-Time Data Access & Automation,"I’ve been drawn to the idea of scaling and automating from a very young age and it repeatedly drives my view of how to make things work better. From my varied experiences I’ve seen a unifying pattern. 

Whether the goal is improving care, accelerating trials, reducing operational burden, managing the back office, or scaling proven health innovations, progress is always held back by the same underlying challenges: the inability to intelligently and automatically use data. And it shows up everywhere:
•	In large health systems trying to automate care processes
•	In financially strained organizations working to minimize losses and seeking efficiencies 
•	In implementation-science teams trying to monitor fidelity
•	In clinical trialists trying to activate sites, identify participants, and track outcomes
•	In innovators trying to integrate digital tools into everyday workflows
•	In translational research endeavors bringing the best ideas to clinical and population care

I’ve spent more than four decades working on these challenges from multiple vantage points:
•	Academic researcher (400+ publications) focused on health problems and care models
•	Health-system R&D leader (Geisinger, Sutter) building digital health solutions, advanced analytics, machine learning, biobanking, and population health models
•	Clinical trial innovator (IMR) cutting Phase III OTC trial time by 66% 
•	Chairing Merit Review committees of translational research proposals (PCORI) and seeing how infrastructure gaps constrain what is possible with even the strongest intervention designs
•	Entrepreneur solving EHR data interoperability (Medcurio) to make automation real

The same insight always emerges: Translation, automation, and scaling all depend on fluid, governed, secure but unconstrained real-time access to EHR data. Without that, most everything we do and will continue to do is manual, slow, and unscalable.

I co-founded Medcurio to enable others to unleash the best ideas and rapidly bring them to practice by removing the integration barriers that have slowed healthcare for decades. Our no-code API technology enables health systems and innovators to do just that, to build real-time, automated workflows without IT bottlenecks.

This is not a distant vision. It is working today. If you’re exploring automation, trial efficiency, care-model redesign, or translational implementation—and you suspect data access is your hidden constraint—I’m always open to a conversation.

You can reach me at buzz@medcurio.com.",Yes,,,,,,United States,New Hampshire,Portsmouth,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/buzzstewart,Medcurio,2-10,11,hospitals and health care,,"Medcurio gives healthcare systems secure on-demand access to all of their EHR data. Get easy access to any data you need to improve the quality and reduce the cost of financial, administrative and clinical operations with our proven interoperability platform. Build, test and deploy no code APIs in hours - at a fraction of today's cost - and stay ahead of unexpected data changes with automated change detection.

Explore what's possible when you can easily deliver your data where you want it in real time.",https://www.medcurio.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/medcurio,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,,SEED,medcurio.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
