Jason,Morton,CEO/President,Prospect Life Sciences,"CEO/President, Prospect Life Sciences | 29yrs Medical Device Development & Manufacturing","I started Prospect Life Sciences in 2016, because after 20+ years in the Medical Device industry, I knew there had to be a better way to help Device and Biotech companies bring their products to production.

I was positive, because at each stage of my career, I’d had a front row seat to what could go wrong at each stage…

– Complications with compliance and proving safety/effectiveness
– Project management that fell short when it came to deadlines
– Budgets that ran over and caused the project to fail
– Manufacturer transfer that dropped the ball on quality, cost, etc

And I had just as many opportunities to see what could go right…

If only I could control more of the process. 

So after working in product development, contract R&D, and product management, I set out to fill in the gaps and learn everything there was to know about taking a new device from an idea all the way into production. 

I got my MBA to learn the financing, accounting, budgeting and pricing of a product. 

I joined a startup, so I could put all the components together, and through that experience, I learned about clinical trials, investors, the considerations around funding, and just how easy it can be for a startup to fail in the “normal” process of bringing a product to market.

That galvanized my decision to offer a better way, and in 2016, we opened the doors to Prospect Life Sciences in Westminster, Colorado.

Since then, we’ve specialized in helping innovative device firms bring their devices to market.

– For startups, that often means helping them achieve compliance and collecting the data they need to get their next stage of funding

– For early stage companies, our focus is often on controlling their costs, making the most of their margins, and protecting their valuation by extending their capacity without additional capital expenditures

– And for the more established firms - we help them expand their product lines and reach their growth goals faster – without having to build additional capacity (or new teams of experts) in-house

PLS can support your team through the entire process, from device development through manufacturing, quality control, supply chain, and fulfillment.

For us, this is the fun part.

And if you’re looking for a manufacturing partner who cares as much about seeing your device get to market as you do – we’d be eager to speak with you and your team.

To learn more:

– Message me here on LinkedIn
– Visit our website: www.prospectlifesciences.com
– Or feel free to email me at jason@prospectlifesciences.com",No,,,,,,United States,Colorado,Denver Metropolitan Area,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/jason-morton-b4020111,Prospect Life Sciences,11-50,11,medical equipment manufacturing,,"We take pride in improving the performance and safety of new medical devices including sterile single use, electromechanical, combination and diagnostic kit products. 

