Robyn,Frisch,Founder/CEO,Rochem International Inc.,"CEO at Rochem Interntational, Inc.","As the founder and CEO of Rochem International, I’ve had the privilege of building a global business that connects top manufacturers and regulated markets worldwide. My journey began 30 years ago when I left China to pursue the American Dream. Arriving in NY with empty pockets, but a heart of determination, I used my education in chemical and pharmaceutical raw materials to create something meaningful.

“To me, America was a vast ocean where fish could swim freely, and every horizon held limitless possibilities.”

What began in a basement in Bayside, Queens, NY, grew into a company supplying high-quality ingredients to the pharmaceutical, food, beverage, nutritional, and cosmetic industries.
My vision was simple: bring high-quality ingredients from China to North America. Rochem now has operating offices and warehouses in North America, Europe, and China, offering leading products and regulatory services to global companies.

We became pioneers, introducing Chinese-origin materials to U.S. and EU markets. In 1997, I introduced xylitol from China to the U.S. In 2000, I filed the first DMF for paclitaxel, an anti-cancer drug. By 2002, we brought products like benzocaine and DC vitamins B1 and B2 to regulated markets.

In 2014, we expanded with a 60,000 sq. ft. HQ in Hauppauge, NY, in the second-largest industrial park in the U.S. With sales offices in France, Italy, Germany, and 8 U.S. locations, our global presence continues to grow. I’m proud of our dedicated team in Qingdao, China, who’ve supported us since 2005. This team of over 20 regulatory compliance experts continues to play a vital role in our operations.

Despite challenges—starting a business and frequent travel between China and New York—I’ve learned that strong partnerships and company culture drive success. We’re passionate about creating value for our partners, and our commitment to excellence is reflected in awards like the Supplier Excellence Award and recognition as one of Long Island’s Power Women.

Today, my focus is expanding into new healthcare sectors and driving growth in emerging markets, while continuing innovation in our current industries. While honored by Rochem’s recognition, I remain dedicated to our team's passion, resilience, and hard work, and to maintaining our commitment to integrity, innovation, and excellence. I’m grateful to lead a company built on trust and a vision for lasting impact.

