Her career began in pharmaceutical research and development and evolved into high-impact leadership roles across academia, healthcare, and the life sciences. As Assistant Vice President of Research Administration at Emory University, she led environmental health and safety efforts and played a critical role on Emory’s Team Ebola. During the treatment of patients with Ebola virus disease, she helped establish new standards for high-consequence pathogen response.

