Matthew,Nuñez,Chief Executive Officer,MUSE Microscopy Inc,"Chief Executive Officer @ MUSE Microscopy Inc | Molecular Diagnostics, Biotechnology","Matthew Nuñez
CEO and Director of MUSE Microscopy, Inc.

Matthew Nuñez is an accomplished entrepreneur and visionary leader with over 25 years of experience, including the last 15 years dedicated to advancing healthcare innovations. As the CEO and Director of MUSE Microscopy, Inc., Matthew is at the helm of a company redefining the future of pathology with groundbreaking solutions that transform how clinicians, researchers, and healthcare systems approach diagnostics and patient care.

MUSE Microscopy: Breaking 125 Years of Tradition in Pathology
Under Matthew’s leadership, MUSE Microscopy is taking a bold and transformative approach to digital pathology with its revolutionary SmartPath Imager, the first tissue-to-digital imaging system powered by MUSE technology. The SmartPath Imager addresses fundamental limitations in traditional pathology workflows, which for over 125 years have relied on destructive slide-based histology—a process requiring tissue samples to be sliced, stained, and permanently altered before examination under a microscope.

The SmartPath Imager can eliminate the need for this labor-intensive and time-consuming preparation by offering a non-destructive, tissue-to-digital imaging solution. Using advanced ultraviolet (UV) imaging technology, the system captures high-resolution digital images directly from fresh or unprocessed tissue samples. This innovation preserves the integrity of the tissue, allowing for additional testing, re-evaluation, and a comprehensive diagnostic approach that is impossible with conventional methods.

SmartPath's Key Innovations and Advantages:

Non-Destructive Workflow: By preserving tissue in its natural state, the SmartPath Imager enables clinicians to conduct additional molecular or genetic tests on the same sample, empowering multi-modal diagnostics.
Rapid Imaging: Produces high-resolution digital images within minutes, significantly reducing the delay between sample collection and diagnosis, which traditionally takes days or weeks.
Enhanced Diagnostic Precision: The technology retains cellular details critical for precise diagnostics, making it ideal for applications in oncology, women’s health, and veterinary pathology.
First-to-Market Advantage: As the first commercially available tissue-to-digital imaging system, MUSE’s SmartPath Imager is uniquely positioned to set new standards in digital pathology.",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,Irvine,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/matthew-nuñez-081a1621,MUSE Microscopy Inc,11-50,8,biotechnology research,,MUSE Microscopy's SmartPath MUSE Technology (SmartPath) Instrument is a transformative digital instrument that generates digital tissue images within minutes. This technology uses a nondestructive water-based solution that can be sent to a pathologist anywhere in the world for a quick read.,http://www.musemicroscopy.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/muse-microscopy-inc,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,,,musemicroscopy.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
