Rami,Elghandour,Chairman & Chief Executive Officer,Arcellx,Chairman & CEO of Arcellx | Gender Equity + Human Rights Advocate | Views my own,"Rami Elghandour is Chairman and CEO of Arcellx (NASDAQ: ACLX), a biotechnology company developing transformative immunotherapies for cancer and autoimmune diseases. Rami has led two successful IPOs, built two multibillion-dollar public companies, and raised more than $1.75 billion in capital.Since joining in 2021, Rami transformed Arcellx from a small, early-stage startup into a leading, commercial-ready organization. During his tenure, he advanced anito-cel, the best therapeutic option for multiple myeloma, and drove a more than fortyfold increase in value with its acquisition by Gilead for $8.2 billion in April 2026. Previously, Rami was President and CEO of Nevro Corporation (formerly NYSE: NVRO), a global medical device company. Rami scaled the company from 30 employees to nearly 1,000, increasing its value by more than tenfold and reaching a peak valuation of over $3 billion.Rami’s career has spanned research, investing, and leadership roles with a dedication to bringing innovative, best-in-class therapies to patients and clinicians. He started his career as a design engineer designing and developing implantable neurostimulators. As a venture capitalist with Johnson and Johnson Development Corporation, he invested in next-generation advances across devices, biotechnology, and consumer products.A recognized champion of diversity and inclusion, Rami has cultivated high performance teams through intentional representation of women and diverse leaders. He’s consistently earned recognition as an EY Entrepreneur of the Year, as one of the top CEOs in the U.S. , and as a top CEO for women, diversity, and culture. He has also received the Bill Campbell Award, the Diversity Woman Magazine Game Changer Award, and the BLOC 100 Champion Award for his advocacy on behalf of women and women of color. Rami is a TEDx speaker on unconscious bias and is recognized voice on gender equity.Rami is also a passionate advocate for social justice. He writes and speaks often on social issues, and is an executive producer on multiple award-winning films, including the Oscar-nominated “The Voice of Hind Rajab” and “American Doctor”, which premiered at the Sundance Film Festival. He serves on multiple nonprofit boards dedicated to advancing education, gender equity, and humanitarian impact.    Rami received an MBA from the Wharton School of the University of Pennsylvania and holds a BS in Electrical and Computer Engineering from Rutgers University School of Engineering.",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,San Francisco Bay Area,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/ramielghandour,Arcellx,51-200,236,biotechnology research,,We are a clinical-stage biotechnology company reimagining cell therapy through the development of innovative immunotherapies.,http://arcellx.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/arcellx,PUBLIC_COMPANY,0,10000000-25000000,621999986,POST_IPO_EQUITY,arcellx.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
Reginald,Swift,Founder & CEO,Rubix LS,"Founder & CEO, Rubix LS | Clinical Research & Evidence Generation | Precision Medicine, RWE, HEOR & Health Equity | Board Advisor","I’m the Founder &amp; CEO of Rubix LS, a clinical research and evidence-generation company focused on helping life sciences, biotech, pharma, diagnostics, and public health partners turn scientific concepts into executable research programs.My work sits at the intersection of clinical trial strategy, biomarker evidence, regulatory readiness, real-world data, HEOR, and health equity. Rubix LS designs and executes research programs that support therapeutic development, diagnostic validation, patient access, and evidence generation for populations that have historically been underserved or underrepresented in clinical research.With a foundation in mechanical engineering and multidisciplinary product development, I bring a systems-level approach to clinical research. That includes protocol development, site strategy, mobile and community-based trial models, data infrastructure, compliance readiness, and partner-facing evidence strategy.Current Rubix LS priorities include oncology, women’s health, neurodegenerative disease, AI-enabled precision medicine, environmental exposure-linked disease risk, and real-world evidence programs that connect research execution to measurable patient impact.My focus is simple: build research architecture that is scientifically credible, operationally executable, and representative of the patients innovation is meant to serve.For strategic partnerships, clinical research collaborations, and evidence-generation opportunities, contact me at rswift@rubixls.com",Yes,,,,,,United States,Massachusetts,Greater Boston,founder,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/rswift,Rubix LS,11-50,10,biotechnology research,,"Rubix LS is a clinical research and evidence generation company. We design studies, run trials, and produce real-world evidence using data from the patient populations most underrepresented in today's research.

We work across the full development lifecycle with biotech sponsors, pharmaceutical companies, and federal health agencies. Our teams bring scientific depth, operational discipline, and access to patient populations that most organizations can't reach.

What we do:

Translational Research and Evidence Strategy
We help sponsors identify evidence gaps early and build study designs that hold up through regulatory review and payer evaluation. Our work includes feasibility assessments, biomarker strategy, endpoint selection, and integrated evidence plans shaped by data from 25M+ patient records across underserved communities. Therapeutic areas include oncology, rare disease, and infectious disease.

Clinical Trial Services
Full-service CRO from pre-clinical studies through Phase II, with partnered Phase III/IV support. We handle protocol development, regulatory strategy, site management, patient recruitment, safety monitoring, data management, and biostatistics. Our mobile clinical sites extend trial access to communities that traditional site networks don't reach, supporting 90% retention in hard-to-reach populations.

Federal Health and Public Health Research
We partner with federal agencies on infectious disease surveillance, biodefense programs, and community health initiatives, bringing the same scientific rigor we apply to commercial programs combined with experience navigating federal contracting and culturally informed engagement strategies.

Our research programs draw on 25M+ integrated patient data sets representing communities, geographies, and disease presentations that are systematically absent from standard clinical databases. That data foundation changes what we can measure, who we can study, and how strong the resulting evidence is.

