Frank,Borriello,CEO,Alloplex Biotherapeutics Inc,Founder and CEO at Alloplex Biotherapeutics Inc.,"Scientific Founder &amp; CEO | Building Next-Generation Autologous Cell TherapiesAboutA physician-scientist with a data-driven approach who trained at the Albert Einstein College of Medicine in NYC and pursued post-graduate studies at the Brigham and Women’s Hospital in Boston. Following a brief academic career, transitioned into the financial and pharma industries taking roles clinical development, business development, and external asset evaluation at Wyeth, BB Biotech, Millennium, Takeda, Shire, and Baxalta.Following an industry consolidation event, founded Alloplex Biotherapeutics in 2015 to bring forward an original approach to cell immunology which after 10 years of effort, led to the first clinical stage, SUPLEXA, an autologous, non-engineered PBMC-derived cellular immunotherapy designed to leverage natural biological mechanisms. This first-in-human Phase 1 clinical trial focused on end-stage metastatic solid tumor patients was successfully completed in Australia. The results demonstrated a robust manufacturing process for a cell therapy product that yielded both single-agent activity as assessed by stringent RECIST criteria and a pristine safety profile. Key observations from the clinical study, including the surprising impact of SUPLEXA on bone marrow to mitigate the number of immune suppressive cells in the circulation of treated patients along with a new appreciation that SUPLEXA cells specifically migrate to bone marrow and lymphatics. These findings have led to a reoriented strategy that prioritizes hematologic malignancies, (e.g., MM, AML, MDS). Subsequent constructive FDA Pre-IND dialogue, we have submitted our first IND to support U.S. development for SUPLEXA in a solid tumor indication with plans to prepare additional INDs in hematologic oncology indications. My focus is now to build a lasting company grounded in biological rationale, operational discipline and thoughtful capital strategy. We are actively engaging family offices, institutional investors and strategic partners aligned with advancing an individualized and safe approach to immune cell therapy with applications in oncology, autoimmunity and potential general chronic low level inflammatory settings related to aging. With a clinically derisked Phase 2-ready program, Alloplex is seeking financial and strategic partners to continue a targeted clinical development program in indications of significant high unmet medical need and commercial potential.Learn more about Alloplex at alloplexbio.com",Yes,,,,,,United States,Massachusetts,Woburn,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/frankborriello,Alloplex Biotherapeutics Inc,2-10,5,biotechnology research,,Alloplex Biotherapeutics is dedicated to exploring the higher order combinatorial space of immunomodulators to develop an effective anti-tumor vaccine. This approach is applicable to all tumor types and is particularly suited to combinations with checkpoint inhibitors. Alloplex is a private company and currently supported by angel investment,https://alloplexbio.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/alloplex-biotherapeutics,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,100000-500000,,,alloplexbio.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
