When it is time to recharge you can find me on one of my local mountain biking or hiking trails.  I am still developing my palate for beer, wine and tequila and always open to recommendations.",No,,,,,,United States,New Mexico,Corrales,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/carlos-perea-12227,Terra Vera,2-10,14,biotechnology research,,"Terra Vera is a biomimetic oxidant technology platform advancing how industries manage biological stress, environmental threats, and system resilience.

Our science is inspired by natural immune responses. Using activated amino acid–based oxidative chemistry, we generate controlled oxidants that work through multi-target mechanisms designed to reduce resistance pressure while breaking down into naturally occurring compounds.

We are building a scalable oxidative biotechnology platform with applications across agriculture, apiculture, environmental systems, and public health.

𝗔𝗽𝗶𝗩𝗲𝗿𝗮™ | 𝗔𝗱𝘃𝗮𝗻𝗰𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗛𝗼𝗻𝗲𝘆 𝗕𝗲𝗲 𝗛𝗲𝗮𝗹𝘁𝗵

Our flagship application, ApiVera™, focuses on one of the most urgent challenges in global agriculture: honey bee health.

Commercial beekeepers face what are often called the 4 P’s to Colony Health (by Dr. Jeff Pettis):

• Parasites (e.g., Varroa)
• Pathogens
• Poor Nutrition
• Pesticide exposure

These compounding stressors contribute to colony losses and long-term instability.

ApiVera’s oxidative approach is designed to support colony resilience by addressing parasites and pathogens through controlled biomimetic oxidation — without introducing persistent synthetic residues or single-target chemistry that can accelerate resistance.

Our goal is not just treatment, but long-term biological resilience aligned with modern apiculture and resistance management strategies.

𝗘𝘅𝗽𝗮𝗻𝗱𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗣𝗹𝗮𝘁𝗳𝗼𝗿𝗺 𝗔𝗽𝗽𝗹𝗶𝗰𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝘀

Beyond honey bee health, Terra Vera’s oxidant technology platform is being developed for:

• Specialty crop systems
• Structural pest environments
• Bed bug remediation
• Water systems and environmental disinfection
• Animal and public health applications

Terra Vera is building next-generation oxidative biotechnology designed for safety, adaptability, and global deployment.

We partner with beekeepers, researchers, growers, and strategic collaborators worldwide.",https://terravera.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/terra-vera-corp,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,2479000,SEED,terravera.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
