Mit,"Desai, MD",Chief Executive Officer,The Surgicalist Group,Surgeon-entrepreneur delivering innovative hospital based care to hospitals nationwide,"I graduated from the University of Michigan, Ann Arbor with a B.S with Honors in Microbiology in 1992 and Wayne State University School of Medicine in 1997.  My residency was at UIC-MGH in Chicago, where I was the Chief Resident and Surgical Resident Teacher of the year. I received my certification from The American Board of Surgery in 2004 and re-certified in 2012. I am also a Fellow of the American College of Surgeons, and have been for over 10 years. I have written numerous publications and have received awards for my achievements.  I am currently the Principal/CEO of The Surgicalist Group.",No,,,,,,United States,Florida,Greater Tampa Bay Area,c_suite,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/drmitdesai,The Surgicalist Group,201-500,22,hospitals and health care,,"The Surgicalist Group is a solution-oriented organization whose model focuses on Trauma, General Surgery, Ortho, GI, Urology services and more. We partner with hospitals nationwide, designing evidence-based programs to meet their needs. In collaboration with the OR, ED, and community physicians, we ensure our partners achieve improved quality, efficiency, patient satisfaction, and financial outcomes.

Established and lead by surgeons since 2007, The Surgicalist Group is uniquely positioned to partner with your hospital in assessing and advising on the clinical, administrative, and logistical goals of your surgical divisions.  Our executive leadership team has an enormous breadth of experience across the healthcare continuum, and does not believe in a ‘one size fits all’ model. Thus, we build personalized programs for each hospital.  

As surgeons ourselves, we are well aware of the gaps inherent to the historic way of providing surgical coverage. When surgeons cover both their elective practice and call duties for the hospital, they simply cannot provide high quality service for both, and the hospital suffers. We see long Emergency Room wait times because a surgeon needs to finish office hours before performing a consult, or the operating room staff has to stay late because the on-call surgeon can’t get to an add-on case until after elective surgeries are completed.  These types of situations lead to decreased patient satisfaction, increased cost and poor outcomes.  This is what we solve!",https://www.thesurgicalist.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-surgicalist-group,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,1000000-5000000,,,thesurgicalist.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
