Gavin,Setzen,Chief Executive Officer,"Albany ENT & Allergy Services, PC","CEO/President, Albany ENT & Allergy | Consulting on growth strategy, operations, high-performing care teams and clinical excellence","As the CEO and President of Albany ENT &amp; Allergy Services, PC, I oversee the largest and most comprehensive independent private practice of ear, nose, and throat specialists in the Capital Region. I am a board-certified otolaryngologist and clinical professor of otolaryngology at Albany Medical Center, where I train and mentor the next generation of surgeons and researchers. I have more than 25 years of experience providing comprehensive care for adult and pediatric patients with disorders of the ears, nose, throat, and related head and neck structures.My special interests include allergy diagnosis and immunotherapy, rhinology, sinus and nasal surgery, and endocrine surgery. I am a past president and fellow of the American Academy of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery, a Director of the American Board of Otolaryngology-Head &amp; Neck Surgery, and a member of several other professional societies and organizations. I am a Fellow of the American Academy of Otolaryngic Allergy, the American College of Surgeons, the American Rhinologic Society, and the American Head &amp; Neck Society, and a Diplomat of the American Board of Otolaryngology.In addition to my clinical, academic, and national leadership roles, I am passionate about helping independent ENT practices and physician leaders think through growth, care model innovation, collaborative team development, audiology, allergy, in-office imaging, ambulatory surgery, payer strategy, health policy, reimbursement, and long-term practice sustainability. Much of this perspective comes from real-world experience helping Albany ENT grow as an independent, physician-led organization while maintaining a strong focus on clinical excellence, patient access, community engagement, and provider collaboration.I also enjoy collaborating with physicians, industry partners, and healthcare organizations on practical innovation in ENT, including care model design, in-office technology, reimbursement strategy, health policy, medtech, and responsible use of AI.I have published multiple articles in peer-reviewed journals and book chapters and have lectured extensively in the United States and internationally. I am passionate about advancing the field of otolaryngology, improving access to high-quality ENT care, and helping physician-led practices remain clinically excellent, operationally strong, and deeply connected to the communities they serve.",No,,,,,,United States,New York,Albany,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/gavinsetzen,"Albany ENT & Allergy Services, PC",51-200,91,hospitals and health care,,"We provide comprehensive care of Pediatric and Adult patients with medical and surgical problems involving the Ears, Nose, Throat and related Head and Neck structures.

Dr. Gavin Setzen obtained his medical degree in Johannesburg, South Africa. After spending 2½ years in general surgery at North Shore University Hospital, Cornell University Medical College, he completed a five-year residency in Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgery at Albany Medical Center in Albany, NY.

Dr. Setzen is a Diplomat of the American Board of Otolaryngology and Fellow of the American-Academy of Otolaryngology-Head and Neck Surgeons(AAO-HNS), the American College of Surgeons, the American Academy of Otolaryngic Allergy the American Rhinologic Society & the American Head and Neck Society. He is active in resident teaching, clinical research and several local and national medical & non-medical organizations. Dr. Setzen is an assistant clinical professor of Otolaryngology-Head & Neck Surgery at Albany Medical Center.

Dr. Setzen is President of the New York State Society of Otolaryngology- Head & Neck Surgery. He is immediate Past-Chair of the Board of Governors of the American Academy of Otolaryngology- Head and Neck Surgery. He serves on the Board of Directors of the Intersocietal Commission for the Accreditation of CT Laboratories and is President-Elect of ICACTL. 

Dr. Setzen is involved with several not-for-profit organizations and is President-Elect of Jewish Federation of Northeastern New York.",http://www.albanyentandallergy.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/albany-ent-&-allergy,SELF_OWNED,0,5000000-10000000,,,albanyentandallergy.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
Joseph,Kitonga,Founder & CEO,Vitable Health,"Founder & CEO, Vitable Health | Thiel Fellow","I immigrated from Kenya to Philadelphia at 13 when my family won the lottery. My father, a teacher in Kenya, cashed out his pension to buy one-way tickets for us to come to the U.S. We arrived with just our suitcases, each other, and not much else, moving into a small basement apartment in inner-city Philadelphia.

Living in a city where just five miles can mean a twenty-year difference in life expectancy, I saw early how unequal access to care shapes people’s lives. My parents worked tirelessly, bootstrapping a home care business from nothing. I saw firsthand the sacrifices they made to support our family and the struggles their employees faced. Many were hourly workers who earned too much for Medicaid but too little to afford comprehensive health insurance. Even when my parents offered to cover half of the premiums, most could not afford to opt in. Without coverage, they often relied on the ER for preventable health issues, which led to delayed care and worse outcomes.

Determined to change that reality, I dropped out of Penn State as a Thiel Fellow to build Vitable Health with the mission to give hourly and blue-collar workers and the small businesses that employ them access to affordable, high-quality care. We combine ICHRA administration with direct primary care, delivering virtual visits, over 1,000 prescriptions, and more than 40 lab tests for free with no copays or deductibles. We manage the entire experience, from onboarding and plan selection to high-touch care employees actually use.

When I am not building Vitable, you might find me savoring a Philly cheesesteak, strumming my guitar, or taking long walks along the Philadelphia waterfront.",Yes,,,,,,United States,California,San Francisco,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/josephkitonga,Vitable Health,51-200,106,hospitals and health care,,"We asked ourselves — What if better care didn’t cost more?

That’s why we built Vitable: the health benefits platform making healthcare better for employers of everyday workers.
 We bring accessible, high-quality care to over 85 million uninsured and underinsured Americans. Unlike traditional options, our suite of health benefits is designed with real people at the center.

Vitable empowers businesses to become better employers by making it easy to offer healthcare benefits to their teams. Vitable is a better experience for employees and a smarter solution for employers. 
Simply put, we’re built for better.",https://vitablehealth.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/vitable-health,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,5000000-10000000,24800000,SERIES_A,vitablehealth.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
