Leonard,"Jensen MSN, FNP-C",Chief Executive Officer,FireNote,"Co-Founder & Chief Executive Officer, FireNote | MSN, FNP-C & Palliative Care","Leonard “Lenny” Jensen, MSN, FNP-C, is a visionary healthcare leader and entrepreneur dedicated to transforming end-of-life care through innovative technology and compassionate service. With over 24 years of experience, he combines deep clinical expertise with technological acumen to address critical challenges in geriatric, palliative, and hospice care.

Lenny began his distinguished 16-year career in the U.S. Army at age 18, enlisting as a Private. Over five years, he achieved the rank of Sergeant, which led to the highly competitive Green to Gold scholarship. He utilized this opportunity to earn his BSN and commission as an officer in the Army Nurse Corps, later earning his MSN. Throughout his service, he honed specialized skills in acute care, intensive care, mental health, and leadership.

His transition to entrepreneurship began in 2006 when, alongside his wife Marianne, he co-founded Serenity hospice and in 2013 Keystone Health and Keystone Hospice. Identifying severe inefficiencies in existing EMR systems—which led to nurse burnout and reduced patient time—Lenny and his team launched FireNote beta in 2020. Under his leadership, FireNote grew exponentially, becoming adopted nationwide. Key achievements include reducing documentation time for new patient admissions from up to four hours to just 45 minutes, enabling better patient-provider interactions, and positioning Keystone Hospice to manage COVID-19 patients safely during the pandemic.

Lenny holds a Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from the University of Alabama at Birmingham and is a Certified Family Nurse Practitioner (FNP-C), specializing in Palliative Care and Geriatric Medicine. He regularly attends Harvard’s annual Geriatric Conference and is an active member of the AANP, NNBA, and AGS. To fully integrate his clinical and organizational skills with technology, he completed the MIT 29-Week Tech CEO Program.

He leads with a commitment to ethical innovation and human-centered care, particularly for seniors and veterans. His contributions have revolutionized hospice EMR systems, fostering seamless continuity of care. Recognized as a thought leader, he shares insights on healthcare technology and veteran care through industry conferences.",No,,,,,,United States,Idaho,Eagle,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/leonard-jensen-msn-fnp-c-b3861821,FireNote,51-200,38,hospitals and health care,,FireNote is a Hospice-First EMR platform that has successfully reduced time spent charting by over 70%. FireNote has taken the challenges of hospice documentation head on and is effectively enhancing the quality of the final result.,https://firenote.health,https://www.linkedin.com/company/firenote,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,1000000-5000000,,,firenote.health,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
