Alex,Kurian,Co-Founder & Chief Executive Officer,Nurocoach,"Co-Founder & CEO, Nurocoach | Building integrated psychiatric care infrastructure for pain medicine and beyond","The mental health burden in a typical pain management practice is not a peripheral issue. Based on analysis of nearly 20,000 neuromodulation candidate intakes, close to 60% of chronic pain patients likely have a PHQ-9 score of 15 or above. More than 80% self-report being on psychotropic medication. 1 in 13 report past or present suicidal ideation.

These are not edge cases. They are the majority of the patient population.

And they are the patients most at risk for poor procedural outcomes, low satisfaction scores, and costly churn—not because their pain isn't being treated, but because no one is treating the whole person.

That's the gap I set out to close when we founded Nurocoach.

What Nurocoach does:
Nurocoach is a national psychiatric practice built specifically to integrate with the practices that see the highest-burden patients — pain management, bariatric surgery, primary care — and provide the psychiatric infrastructure those practices need but aren't built to deliver themselves.

We bring behavioral health integration (BHI) models, embedded clinical teams, TMS, Spravato, medication management, and therapy to patients who are already in the care system — just not getting the full picture of what they need.

We operate brick-and-mortar clinics in Sugar Land and Bryan/College Station, Texas. We provide telehealth psychiatric care across 25 states. We hold 75+ insurance contracts and accept 45+ plans — because access only works if the financial barriers come down too.

Our clinical model has been validated across 80,000+ chronic pain patient engagements.

My background:
Before Nurocoach, I spent years working with some of the world's leading organizations as a business developer, performance consultant, and research partner — across healthcare, technology, retail, and financial services.

That generalist foundation turned out to be exactly the right preparation for building something that lives at the intersection of clinical care, insurance infrastructure, regulatory compliance, and operational scale.
I think about healthcare access as a systems problem. The clinical model has to be right. The billing infrastructure has to work. The partnerships have to be built on trust, not just referral agreements. And the data has to tell the story that words can't.

If you're building or operating a pain management practice, bariatric program, or health system and want to talk about what behavioral health integration could look like for your patient population—I'm genuinely interested in the conversation. Let's talk.",Yes,,,,,,United States,,Greater Houston,founder,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/alex-kurian-257b751,Nurocoach,11-50,20,mental health care,,"Nurocoach is a national multi-specialty medical practice with a mission to break through barriers of access to mental health care. As the mental health crisis in America continues to worsen, we believe that access is imperative. This means convenient telehealth appointments so you can meet where you are most comfortable. Financial access to care, means that we accept many insurances and we have appointments available within 48 hours. We are proud to support anyone struggling with anxiety, depression, sleep disorders, ADHD or other mental health challenges. We are proud to offer a range of services from cognitive behavioral (CBT) therapy, nutrition and sleep counseling, and innovative treatments such as TMS. We partner with NPs, PAs, DOs and MDs at primary care, pain and other specialty practices to support patients and report on their progress through our proprietary NuroChart.",http://www.nurocoach.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/nurocoach,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,500000-1000000,,,nurocoach.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
