Hannan,Lis,Chairman and Co-Founder,Zera Medical,"Business owner and Investor in service, real estate, education, manufacturing and technology businesses.","Business owner and Investor in service, real estate, education, manufacturing  and technology businesses. Significant involvement and interest in community development, public service and economic development. Business and not-for-profit involvement in the USA and Israel.  Committed to the prosperity and success of the United States, the State of Michigan and Israel.",No,,,,,,United States,Michigan,Clawson,founder,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/hannanlis,Zera Medical,2-10,6,medical equipment manufacturing,,"Colorectal cancer is one of the most preventable diseases in America. Yet screening rates have stalled, not because of awareness or access, but because of the prep.

For decades, patients have been asked to manage bowel preparation at home: days of dietary restriction, large volumes of harsh laxatives, and an uncomfortable, uncertain experience with no guarantee of adequate results. For millions of eligible adults, this is the reason screening is delayed, or avoided entirely.

The impact is significant. Inadequate preparation affects an estimated 18–35% of colonoscopies, contributing to missed lesions, repeat procedures, same-day cancellations, and substantial costs across the healthcare system.

Zera Medical is building a better way. Our flagship system, ZeraFlow, is a clinic-based, nurse-supervised warm-water bowel preparation performed immediately before colonoscopy. By shifting prep from an uncontrolled home setting into a standardized clinical workflow, we aim to improve consistency, patient experience, and clinical outcomes.

ZeraFlow is currently pursuing FDA 510(k) clearance and has been validated through real-world clinical use internationally, demonstrating strong safety and cleansing adequacy.

We are a U.S.–Israel MedTech team on a mission to remove the single greatest barrier between patients and life-saving preventive care.

