Angela,"Carrillo, CIP, NLP, BA",CEO,Brass Tacks Recovery,Interventionist | Speaker | Mental Health Coach |    I invite a deeper conversation for women and men about exploring and healing the places we hide ~ inside and outside of ourselves ~ in relationships and careers.,"The truth is that my brokenness has become my strength. I never imagined that the trauma of addiction and abandonment I experienced in childhood would be the fire that would shape my ability to help families heal. Having lived through these challenges firsthand, I know how painful it is to watch someone you love struggle with addiction or mental health issues. My personal losses have fueled my commitment to becoming the expert I wish I’d had in my own life.

As a child, I lost my biological mother to alcoholism and addiction. Growing up in a dysfunctional family, I faced developmental trauma that shaped my early years. Despite being an honor student with much potential, I began using drugs and alcohol at the age of 12, unable to cope with my emotions. My addiction eventually overtook my academic pursuits, leading me to drop out of college after my first semester. For a while, I lived in my car, moving from one couch to another to survive. In search of a solution, I enlisted in the U.S. Army at 19, hoping the military could change me. Instead, my alcoholism worsened.

As the CEO and Founder of Brass Tacks Recovery, I lead with integrity and compassion. I hold certifications as a Certified Intervention Professional (CIP), Practitioner of Neuro-Linguistic Programming (NLP), Certified Professional Coach (CPC), and PIVOT Certified Relational Coach. I use trauma and attachment-informed approaches to help clients and their families. I’ve also served on the Board of Directors for the Women’s Association for Addiction Treatment (WAAT) and held leadership positions with the Los Angeles International Association of Eating Disorders (IAED LA). In 2016, I earned my BA in Psychology from Antioch University.

Brass Tacks Recovery is the culmination of my personal and professional journey. From this experience, I developed one of our most effective tools, the Coach To Intervene (CTI)™ method. This approach equips families with the knowledge and skills they need to support their loved ones while preparing themselves for the intervention process. CTI serves as the initial phase of family system recovery, aligning the family’s readiness with thoughtful and informed action.

Watch for my upcoming book, Exploring…the Places We Hide: Healing and Integrating the Pieces Within, where I share my story of addiction to recovery ~ and beyond ~ but perhaps most importantly, where I invite a deeper conversation for all women and men about the places we hide ~ inside and outside of ourselves ~ in relationships, in our jobs, in our busyness, and more.",No,,,,,,United States,California,Los Angeles,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/angelahelpsheal,Brass Tacks Recovery,2-10,11,mental health care,,"Brass Tacks Recovery offers intervention and family support services, client case management, recovery/life integration coaching, and transport services. 

Brass Tacks Recovery combines extensive life skills and experience in the field with an approach based on community, personal care and self-improvement. 

This combination provides a unique support structure that gives our clients the best possible chance at defeating and dealing with their addiction or compulsive behavior. 

What is unique about us is that we work “in the gaps” of what is currently offered in the treatment industry. 

We believe in establishing personal and trusting relationships with our clients and their families in a way that assists not only the family and the client, but also the clinical team.",http://www.brasstacksrecovery.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/brass-tacks-recovery,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,100000-500000,,,brasstacksrecovery.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
