Eric,Race,CEO // Founder,Atlas Mobility,"Founder // CEO, Atlas Mobility | Modern Mobility Solutions: Embedded Mobility Teams, Wearables & Real-Time Data Transforming Hospital Care & ROI Outcomes","I’m the Founder // CEO of Atlas Mobility, based in Miami, FL and San Francisco, CA. Atlas is a healthcare technology company improving mobility, safety, and patient outcomes inside hospitals across the United States. Over the last decade, I’ve built Atlas from the ground up into a nationally deployed clinical operations and FDA registered medical device company with ~400 employees nationwide. We partner with major health systems to reduce injuries, standardize safe patient movement, and modernize how frontline care teams work.

My foundation comes from the emergency field. Before becoming an entrepreneur, I served as a  Stockton firefighter // paramedic and rescue instructor, responding to 911 calls, working in a Level 1 trauma center and training teams in high-risk technical rescue. Those experiences shaped how I operate today: disciplined under pressure, grounded in real-world safety, and committed to building systems that protect people.

That commitment led me to launch Atlas, where we’ve deployed hospital workforce safety programs, developed an FDA-registered medical device, contributed to national safety initiatives (NPIAP, ANA, and others), and helped some of the largest U.S. hospital systems redesign how care teams mobilized patients.

Today, I’m expanding my work toward a broader mission: building the next decade of mobility, Ai and robotics inside healthcare.

Hospitals are entering an era defined by mobile technology, Ai agents, autonomous systems and eventually humanoid-level assistance. My goal is to ensure these technologies are implemented safely, intelligently and in ways that improve the human experience, for both patients and caregivers.

