Adam,"Glendye LPC, CPCS",Founder/CEO,The Pursuit Counseling,"Founder: The Pursuit Counseling | Therapy/Coaching, Ultramarathons, Investor in People","I’m Adam R. Glendye, LPC, CPCS—founder of The Pursuit Counseling, therapist, business owner, and lifelong learner.

I believe every person has a story worth telling—and rewriting. Our lives are not defined by a single moment or decision, but by how we learn, adapt, and grow. That belief is at the core of my practice, my business, and my personal life.

I didn’t go to business school. I went to school to help people. But I’ve embraced the journey of building a thriving group practice—learning through experience, mentorship, and sometimes a bit of “ready, fire, aim” mentality. I’m constantly pursuing growth: in the therapy room, with my team, and as an athlete currently training for an ultramarathon.

I’ve faced my own share of long odds—multiple surgeries and hospitalizations in my youth taught me resilience early. Today, I bring that same perspective to the work I do with individuals, families, and therapists.

Whether you’re a fellow mental health professional, a leader working through transition, or someone on your own pursuit—I’d love to connect, collaborate, and grow together.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Georgia,Fayetteville,founder,"c_suite, consulting",https://www.linkedin.com/in/adamglendye,The Pursuit Counseling,2-10,5,mental health care,,"Therapy isn’t just what happens in the room. It’s what happens before, after, and in between—in the small but powerful moments that shape real change.

At The Pursuit Counseling, we don’t believe in therapy that starts and stops when you walk through a door. We believe in therapy that stays with you.

That’s why we built The Therapy+5 Philosophy. It’s not a technique. It’s not a process. It’s a culture. A way of ‘doing therapy’ that reaches beyond the session and into the fabric of your daily life.

Through personalized experiences, tailored follow-ups, ongoing learning resources, therapeutic spaces, and opportunities for community connection, Therapy+5 creates a space where your mental health remains a priority—inside and outside the therapy room.

We’re not just redefining therapy; we’re redefining how care feels.

The Five Elements of Therapy+5

1- The Five Minutes Before (The Pause Before the Work)

Therapy isn’t something you rush into.

Before your session, we ask you to take five quiet minutes—a pause to check in, to breathe, to notice what’s coming up. No emails. No noise. Just a moment to be.

Because when you walk in already listening to yourself, the work begins before a single word is spoken.

2- The Five Minutes After (Letting It Land)

When therapy ends, the world starts moving again—your phone buzzes, traffic hums, life calls. But before you rush back in, take five minutes to let it land.

3- Personalized Experiences & Tailored Follow-Ups
Therapy should feel like it was built for you—because it is.

4- Purposeful Therapeutic Spaces

Where you do the work matters. That’s why our offices don’t look like sterile clinics—they feel like spaces you actually want to sit in. Kitchen table spaces. Collaborative seating. Rooms designed for real conversations.

5- Community & Connection Beyond the Session

Therapy isn’t just about what happens with your therapist—it’s about who you surround yourself with and how you grow alongside others.",http://www.thepursuitcounseling.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/the-pursuit-counseling,SELF_OWNED,0,100000-500000,,,thepursuitcounseling.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
