Rao,Bezwada,President & CEO,"Bezwada Biomedical, LLC",President of Bezwada Biomedical,"An accomplished scientist and entrepreneur, Rao S. Bezwada, Ph.D. is the founder and president of Bezwada Biomedical, an innovation-based and technology-driven research Company with operations in the United States and India.

The company has focused on developing a wide range of novel absorbable polymeric biomaterials, capable of enhancing the quality of life by producing next-generation bioabsorbable medical devices with therapeutic applications. 

Dr. Bezwada earned a doctorate in chemistry from the Stevens Institute of Technology in New Jersey and has been regarded as a leading expert in the field of bioabsorbable polymers. He has over 35 years of research experience in the medical device industry, including 20 years of service at Ethicon, Inc. (a Johnson & Johnson Company) prior to establishing Bezwada Biomedical in 2003. 

Dr. Bezwada's commitment to medical research is attested to by his original research contributions with critical applications in health care. Specifically, while at Ethicon, his research and development efforts led to the launch of a number of products including Monocryl®, a new ultra-pliable synthetic absorbable monofilament suture. This product has represented worldwide sales of more than ONE (1) billion dollars since its launch in 1993 and current annual sales of over 100 million dollars.

In recognition of this invention, along with its development, Johnson & Johnson, Inc. awarded Dr. Bezwada the prestigious Johnson Medal in 1996. Furthermore, Dr. Bezwada has been a prolific inventor and has been issued more than  120 U.S. patents.

