Zack,Cutler,Product Manager,Boston University Center for Psychiatric Rehabilitation,"Building at the intersection of cognitive science and software · Founder, Kalibrate (iOS, HRV biofeedback) · MBA · Clinical trial + behavioral neuroscience background.","Product builder at the intersection of cognitive science and software.I solo-shipped Kalibrate, a TestFlight iOS application (~28,000 lines of Swift, ~43 test files) that operationalizes the Easterbrook–Yerkes-Dodson attention-arousal framework as a trainable target — pairing multi-object tracking with adaptive difficulty and integrated visual, haptic, and audio stimulation. I also built and bench-validated a feature-gated HRV / respiratory-rate biofeedback layer that pairs with a Bluetooth chest strap (CoreBluetooth, beat-to-beat R-R parsing, RMSSD, RSA-derived respiration estimation).Before Kalibrate, I coordinated a single-blind randomized clinical trial of cognitive training plus exercise in adults with serious mental illness at Boston University's Center for Psychiatric Rehabilitation — administering neuropsychological batteries, managing IRB protocols, building custom scoring software, and co-authoring the resulting publication (McGurk, Otto, Fulford, Cutler et al., 2021, Journal of Psychiatric Research).At BU's Center for Psychiatric Rehabilitation today I own the technical product strategy for the Center's digital products — drove 300%+ growth in lead generation, personally built the Center's blog platform (PHP/HTML/CSS/JS), direct external development teams, and lead the organization-wide website redesign.Background spans clinical-trial coordination in serious mental illness, behavioral neuroscience, full-stack engineering (Launch Academy), and an MBA from Babson (summa cum laude, technology entrepreneurship). I'm a hands-on AI practitioner — Claude Code, Codex, agentic engineering workflows — and I write production code, not just specs.Looking for clinical-product, product-management, or applied-research r