Amy,"Cowperthwait CEO, RN, MSN, CNS, CHSE-A",Founder and CEO | Patient-Centered Simulation Training Authority | 2016 Hayden Vanguard Recipient,Avkin,Founder & CEO | Healthcare Simulation Expert | Clinical Nurse Specialist | Inventor | Speaker | Best University Start-Up,"My journey as founder and CEO of Avkin began in 2015 but my plan to revolutionize healthcare simulation education has been my passion for the last 10 years.

For 28 years, I worked as a nurse in the fast-paced world of the emergency room. I saw every type of patient needing critical and immediate care, and the medical teams did a great job. But I also saw many new nurses – who had solid technical skills – struggle with the real-life matter of truly caring for the person behind the critical need and their family. What was missing in their undergraduate education? The human element. Students were learning procedures on plastic models but their education never included the challenges of communicating with live human patients during their time of greatest need.

I left the emergency room to become a nurse educator and joined the University of Delaware as a clinical faculty member in the School of Nursing (where I still teach). I collaborated with engineering students to create lifelike simulation technology prototypes that would help prepare nursing students, caregivers and patients for invasive  procedures like inserting catheters, IVs and tracheostomy tubes. I also worked with students from the University’s theater department, outfitting them with the prototypes and co-developing a low-cost standardized patient program to ensure there was a live “patient” in every simulation to give realistic responses to learners  practicing procedures on them.

My dream of changing the imbalance between teaching the art and science of healthcare  was coming true. I had invented sensor-enabled, high fidelity, wearable technology for healthcare simulation education, and Avkin was born.

Today, our dedication to patient-centered simulation training remains unwavering. Our products and services are being used in hospitals, nursing schools, and simulation centers nationally and internationally. I am truly excited about the future of Avkin and its impact on care delivery across the globe.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Delaware,Bear,founder,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/amycowperthwait,Avkin,11-50,30,medical equipment manufacturing,,"Avkin is a manufacturer of wearable devices for use in healthcare simulations and is a consultant for standardized patient programs.

Founded by a nurse educator, Avkin provides a simulation solution that combines the best of high-fidelity mannequins and the realism of standardized patients for the most authentic simulation experience possible.

Avkin believes that the key to success in patient-centered care is practitioner training through realistic simulations and that human interaction is irreplaceable in healthcare education. Avkin's sensor-enabled, wearable technology uses haptic feedback to enable a new class of simulation training that teaches both the art (soft skills) and science (hard skills) required from practitioners like doctors, nurses, and first responders.",http://www.avkin.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/avkin,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,1000000-5000000,900000,SEED,avkin.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
