Dr. Mel,"Robinson-Brown, PhD",Founder,"Renewed Focus Psychology Services, PLLC",Unlearn the life you were conditioned to want|Bold Clinical Psychologist & Speaker helping high-achieving women who do it all—and fall apart when no one’s watching.,"Hey there! I’m Dr. Melissa Robinson-Brown, but I go by Dr. Mel — Licensed Clinical Psychologist, speaker, professor, and founder of a multi-six-figure therapy collective.I help high-achieving women who’ve checked every box — degrees, titles, family, accolades — yet still feel stuck inside the life they built.I’m known as The Should Slayer because “shoulds” are inherited expectations that keep women caged — trapped by perfectionism, fear, and rules that were never theirs. I teach women to dismantle those cages, reclaim their power, and build lives rooted in truth, not templates.As a first-generation Trinidadian-American psychologist with 20+ years in the field, I know what it feels like to follow every rule, exceed every expectation, and still lose yourself. I also know toxic workplaces up close — racism, gaslighting, micromanagement, and systems that punish authenticity. I didn’t just study workplace trauma; I survived it.Walking away from my “dream job” ignited my mission to help women stop normalizing toxic work environments — and to help companies build cultures that don’t harm their people.I rebuilt my life from the root, not the résumé, and now lead a multi-six-figure psychology practice delivering culturally attuned, radically honest therapy that transforms women at their core.I headlined Essence Wellness House, and my work has been featured in The New York Times, Vogue, Forbes, HuffPost, DevaCurl, Scary Mommy, and Therapy for Black Girls — proof this message resonates across industries.Today, my work sits at the intersection of mental health, corporate culture, and women’s empowerment. I bring permission energy into every room — freeing women from self-betrayal and reminding them their voice is non-negotiable.I’m a speaker, educator, and disruptor who:• Delivers high-energy keynotes that spark identity-level transformation• Helps companies repair toxic workplace dynamics• Builds corporate wellness programs grounded in emotional safety and cultural competence• Coaches high-achieving women ready to live audaciously• Leads a team providing therapy centered on authenticity and liberationMy approach blends psychology, storytelling, humor, lived experience, and radical truth-telling — culturally grounded conversations that shift how people see themselves and the systems they work in.If you want a speaker who energizes the room, a trainer who transforms culture, or a partner who helps individuals and workplaces heal from the inside out… let’s talk. ✊🏾🔥",Yes,,,,,,United States,New York,New York City Metropolitan Area,founder,"master_information_technology, c_suite",https://www.linkedin.com/in/iamdrmel,"Renewed Focus Psychology Services, PLLC",201-500,7,mental health care,,"In addition to working with women, we also help adolescents deal with emotions and life changes while also helping parents find calm and guidance as they experience their adolescent’s teen years. We strive to help you feel empowered to be your best and most authentic self!

WHAT DO WE OFFER?

Individual Therapy

You can't escape the struggles and confusion of being an adult. There are so many transitions, new experiences to navigate, and it's like no one ever tells you how hard they will be. But we’ll be here for you every step of the way - a shoulder in times when life feels overwhelming, or your career is feeling stuck, someone who celebrates with you on those big accomplishments that make all this worth it! 

Adolescent Counseling

It is a gift to get the chance to work with adolescents. They are smart, witty, and bold people who often exhibit eccentric tendencies that put them at odds with what other adults in their life tell them. It can be exhausting for an adolescent because you want autonomy but still need guidance from someone else. The best way I've found we could help these kids overcome this chaotic experience was when we brought outside perspectives into it - which inspired change!

Parent Coaching

As the world evolves, parents need to be able to relate with their children. Parenting skills coaching is a way of understanding your teen better, whether you're just starting as a first-time parent or are trying to get used to new rules and risks in an evolving world. Ultimately these sessions focus on ensuring that both parents and teenagers have support through what can often be difficult times together.

Ready to talk?

