Michael Reece -,Unified Health Services,Chief Executive Officer,Unified Health Services,Managing the Work Comp Revenue Cycle for Healthcare Providers from Patient Registration to Cash Application,"Unified Health Services specializes in the management of workers' compensation claims for hospitals, surgery centers, and other healthcare organizations. We combine in-depth knowledge of the payor system with technology to create efficient methods of processing work comp claims from patient registration to cash application. This revenue cycle solution drives automation, improved collection rates, fewer unpaid accounts, and lower costs for this unique financial class. Contact me directly or visit www.uhsweb.com for more information.

Since 1997, Unified Health Services has managed 1.14 million work comp patients, representing 2.85 million encounters, and $1.18 billion in work comp A/R for healthcare systems across the U.S.

I graduated from the University of Mississippi with Bachelor and Master Degrees in Accountancy and spent my initial working years with KPMG Peat Marwick. At the time of my departure from the company I was Audit Manager in the Memphis, Tennessee office. In 1993 I joined Leader Federal Bank For Savings as Assistant Controller where I was closely involved in the company's initial public offering. After Leader Federal Bank For Savings was acquired by Union Planters Bank; I joined Third Party Solutions (TPS), a provider of on-line worker's compensation claims processing services for retail pharmacies, as Chief Financial Officer. In 1997 I left TPS to co-found UHS.",No,,,,,,United States,Tennessee,Memphis,c_suite,"c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/michael-reece-unified-health-services-3a58972a,Unified Health Services,51-200,125,hospitals and health care,,"Each year millions of workers are injured on the job and require medical attention. Since worker's compensation is an employee benefit governed by individual states, there are significant and varying rules and regulations involved in processing claims and obtaining reimbursements. Normal billing patterns in healthcare can't be applied to work comp because the nature of processing claims and the payer system is fundamentally different. This unique payor class lacks eligibility systems and invoicing remains a print and mail system burdened by ""attachments""​. The collection process includes phone calls, high invoice submission rates and payment appeals. Finally, reimbursement rates differ by jurisdiction and providers don't know if payments are correct or not.

UHS specializes in end to end management of worker's compensation claims for hospitals, surgery centers, and healthcare systems. We combine an in-depth knowledge of the work comp payor system with technology to create efficient methods of processing work comp claims from patient registration to cash application. Founded in 1997, UHS has managed over 2.1 million work comp patients, 5.7 million encounters, and $7.4 billion in work comp A/R for healthcare systems across the U.S.

We take responsibility for processing work comp claims at patient registration. Our front end solution manages claim verifications and treatment authorizations as well as gathers important claim related information that will be needed to facilitate accurate billing and quick and accurate reimbursement. Healthcare providers bill claims in 837 format through clearinghouses to UHS.  UHS handles the generation and distribution of invoices and performs all collection work.  UHS ensures payments are accurate and cash posting is automated with 835 ERAs.

Results include better collection yields, fewer unpaid accounts, lower A/R, process automation and lower processing costs.

Talk to us about improving your work comp revenue cycle.",http://www.uhsweb.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/unified-health-services,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,5000000-10000000,,,uhsweb.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
