Jessica,Branson,CEO & Executive Director,Positive Directions - The Center for Prevention & Counseling,"Executive Director, Positive Directions- The Center for Prevention & Counseling (Mental Health) | Marketing & Advertising Exec | CPG + Health & Wellness | Beauty | Beverage + Alc Bev |","With 25+ years of business consulting and marketing strategy I've helped scale 4 agencies for acquisition (WPP, Publicis, Dentsu, Omnicom), created award winning work for Coke, Burts Bees, AT&T, Captain Morgan, Jeep, Nestle, Dove, Perrier, Summer's Eve & Dramamine and built my own consultancy, (Branson Growth Consulting (BGC) before my career came to an abrupt halt. 
-During COVID, I became fully paralyzed, contracting Guillain-Barre Syndrome (GBS), a rare neurological disease that affects the peripheral nervous system, hijacking all motor and sensory functions. I went from board rooms to hospital rooms, bedridden, unable to write, feed myself, and wheelchair bound for nearly a year. 
- My trauma unearthed the grit and tenacity to survive, forming a new perspective I will carry forward for life. Now 80% recovered, walking and back to ""normal"" I am newly inspired. I want to share my story to help others. I feel a renewed commitment to create more purposeful work in our professional and personal lives. 
Why Jess?
- Clients appreciate my people-first approach, “on demand” ideas, results driven solutions and transparency.
- Colleagues recognize me as a leader with strong intuition, a keen ability to build relationships & culture and a big picture thinker who can deliver results. 
- Friends describe me as loyal, kind, determined, fierce, funny and generous. 
- My mantra? ""You never know when your story will become someone else’s survival guide"". Brene Brown.
- I am currently an MD at The Shipyard, (Adage Top Independent Agencies) leading media & ecomm for Prestige Consumer Healthcare (Dramamine, Monistat, Summer's Eve, ClearEyes). 
