Kailey,"Fiedler-Gohlke, Ed.D., CRC",Chief Executive Officer,HERO House NW,"Chief Executive Officer @ HERO House NW | Nonprofit Organizations, Behavioral Health","Kailey Fiedler-Gohlke, Ed.D., CRC is the Chief Executive Officer of HERO House NW, a nonprofit organization dedicated to psychiatric rehabilitation through the evidence-based Clubhouse model. Since joining the organization in 2012, Ms. Gohlke has led its strategic growth, expanding its reach across Washington State and advocating for increased investment in behavioral health services.

Ms. Gohlke earned her Bachelor’s degree in Sociology and International Studies from the University of Washington and her Master’s in Rehabilitation Counseling from Western Washington University. She completed her Doctorate of Education in Organizational Leadership from Grand Canyon University in 2025.

A recognized leader in her field, Ms. Gohlke was named a subject matter expert on the Clubhouse model by the Washington State Health Care Authority in 2020. Under her guidance, more than 11 new Clubhouses have launched across the state. She also serves on the Faculty for Clubhouse Development with Clubhouse International, where she travels globally to assess Clubhouse programs for accreditation.

In addition to her leadership at HERO House NW, Ms. Gohlke contributes to the broader behavioral health and rehabilitation community. She serves on the Advisory Board for Western Washington University’s Rehabilitation Counseling program and is a member of King County’s Mental Illness and Drug Dependency (MIDD) Advisory Board. In 2023, she was recognized by the Puget Sound Business Journal as one of the Top 40 Under 40 leaders in the Northwest. Most recently, she was appointed to the State of Washington’s Joint Legislative Executive Committee on Behavioral Health.

Ms. Gohlke lives in Seattle with her husband, their young son, and their beloved cat, Ella. Outside of her professional work, she enjoys traveling the world and spending quality time with her family.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Washington,Seattle,c_suite,c_suite,https://www.linkedin.com/in/kaileyfiedler,HERO House NW,11-50,48,mental health care,,"As an organization we, with our supporters, help people experiencing mental illness in Washington State get jobs, return to school, find affordable housing, and live independent lives.

HERO House NW is a nonprofit, 501(c) 3 organization and is the proud recipient of the 2018 NAMI Seattle's Award for Transformational Leadership. HERO House NW's Clubhouses use a psychiatric rehabilitation model that focuses on socialization and community engagement to bring every participant, known as a “member,” of the clubhouse program to the table for the running of the clubhouse.

This model for rehabilitation is an evidence-based practice that requires adherence to standards set forth by Clubhouse International. Our Clubhouses receive an accreditation visit from Clubhouse International every three years to make sure we are within the best practices of the Clubhouse model. HERO House NW operates three of the four Clubhouses in Washington State, one of more than 180 Clubhouses in the United States, and one of 320 Clubhouses in 34 countries around the world.

HERO House NW's Bellevue Clubhouse has been an accredited member of Clubhouse International since 2008. For more information, see http://clubhouse-intl.org/ In July of 2014, Clubhouse International was selected to receive the Conrad N. Hilton Humanitarian Prize. This is the world’s largest humanitarian prize for extraordinary work to alleviate human suffering by helping people living with mental illness lead productive lives.",http://www.herohousenw.org,https://www.linkedin.com/company/hero-house,NON_PROFIT,0,1000000-5000000,,,herohousenw.org,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
