Ankita,"(Seal) Wheeler, M.S., CCC-SLP",Care Educator,Trualta,"Care Educator at Trualta | Co-Founder, Kindly Neuro | Cognitive Load, Capacity, and Caregiving","I work with caregivers, neurodivergent adults, and professionals who are capable, responsible, and often overwhelmed in ways that are easy to misinterpret.

In my work, I see how being competent often leads to being given more to carry, without anyone checking if the capacity is still there. As responsibilities increase, cognitive and emotional load builds quietly. Over time, people begin to question their motivation, confidence, or sense of self, when the real issue is that the system around them no longer fits.

Much of the advice offered to caregivers and neurodivergent adults focuses on effort, mindset, or self care. What is often missing is an honest look at cognitive load and how sustained responsibility changes what people can realistically carry. Without that lens, even well intentioned guidance can feel like another demand.

I am a Care Educator at Trualta, where I support caregivers through education and facilitation focused on real world challenges. I am also the co founder of Kindly Neuro, where I work on brain aligned strategies that reduce load and support daily functioning.

My current focus is on capacity, cognitive load, and identity under long term responsibility, and what it looks like to design roles and systems that allow people to function without constantly pushing past their limits.",Yes,,,,,,United States,Utah,Salt Lake City,founder,"education, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/ankitawheeler,Trualta,11-50,33,hospitals and health care,,"We empower the most underserved stakeholder in the healthcare system – the family caregiver. 

While training programs exist for home health aides or nurses to help manage care of the elderly, family members, who provide 80%+ of care to loved ones aging-in-place, have limited access to training. For example, actionable education like how to prevent falls in the house, safely transfer from a bed or chair, or manage difficult behaviour when a loved one has dementia. Recognizing that this content exists but isn’t available to families, Trualta adapted professional-level healthcare training for the family member audience. We deliver the training via an informal and interactive online learning environment, and tailor the learning to each caregiver’s situation. The program incentivizes engagement with a rewards system, and users can redeem rewards for helpful products and services. 

Our customers, healthcare payers and providers in Canada & the US, offer Trualta at point-of-care to better enable families to transition aging loved ones from hospital to home, and sustain independent living. Through clinical validation studies in the US and Canada, we are linking participation in Trualta’s program to improved outcomes and reduced costs. We are a proud resident company of the Biomedical Zone in downtown Toronto and the Invest Ottawa Accelerator program.  

If you are passionate about educating and enabling families to improve care for our aging population, drop us a note at info@trualta.com – we’d love to hear from you.",http://www.trualta.com,https://www.linkedin.com/company/trualta,PRIVATELY_HELD,0,1000000-5000000,0,SEED,trualta.com,,,Healthcare founders/owners netnew
