Ryan,Shelton,Co-Founder,"PhotoniCare, Inc.",Co-founder at PhotoniCare | Healthcare Data Strategy & Market Access | Startup Operator | PhD,"I'm a founder, operator, and data strategist who has spent over a decade building a healthcare company from a PhD research project into a commercial-stage medical device business. That experience has given me an unusual combination of skills: I know what it takes to build and run a company, and I know how to turn complex healthcare data into tools that drive real decisions. As Co-founder of PhotoniCare, I've helped lead the company through every stage: product development, FDA clearance, clinical trials, fundraising, team building, and commercialization. Over nine years as CEO, I drove the creation and market support of a new Category III CPT code, building the reimbursement strategy, payer education, and data infrastructure to support patient access, and built the analytical tools that transform raw claims, authorization, and revenue cycle data into dashboards and intelligence that guide commercial decisions. My business expertise spans startup operations, fundraising and capital strategy, strategic planning, team leadership, business development, grant writing, technology licensing, international distribution, and KOL relationship building. My technical foundation is in biomedical engineering (PhD, Texas A&amp;M), and my work has expanded into healthcare data strategy, building AI-powered analytics systems that help healthcare organizations understand payer dynamics, optimize claims processes, and make smarter commercial decisions. I also co-founded Flowfeed, a predictive analytics platform for outdoor athletes, and serve as an NIH SBIR reviewer and board chair at Northwest Health System. Always interested in meeting people working on hard problems in healthcare. Reach out anytime!",No,,,,,,United States,Arkansas,Bentonville,founder,"master_information_technology, c_suite, medical_health",https://www.linkedin.com/in/sheltronica,"PhotoniCare, Inc.",11-50,20,medical equipment manufacturing,,"PhotoniCare was founded out of a shared passion to develop a superior solution for middle ear issues, primarily in children. With $10 billion spent annually to manage ear infections, and a documented 50% misdiagnosis rate for primary care physicians, current tools used to diagnose fluid in the middle ear fail to reliably interpret the patient’s condition. The FDA-cleared OtoSight™ Middle Ear Scope by PhotoniCare is a clinical diagnostic tool designed to eliminate subjectivity and speculation with a non-invasive and comprehensive assessment of middle ear fluid. OtoSight™ is indicated to not only visualize the presence of fluid, but also the fluid’s density, even in the presence of earwax. As a result, the simple-to-use OtoSight™ Middle Ear Scope has a 90+% reader accuracy in determining the presence or absence of fluid in the middle ear. Clinicians that have had an opportunity to use OtoSight™ consider it a game-changer. This is further demonstrated by multiple best-in-show product awards and over 20 supporting clinical publications.  With OtoSight™, PhotoniCare makes the otherwise invisible visible while effectively informing a successful treatment plan like never before.

