• 15–50% initial savings
• 5–20% additional value through ongoing optimization
• Continuous performance monitoring and contract and regulatory enforcement
• No additional workload for employer teams

I’ve spent more than 30 years working across the pharmacy benefits supply chain — PBMs, manufacturers, consulting, and employer programs.

That experience allows me to evaluate pharmacy benefit programs against real market benchmarks, contract structures, and operational models, not vendor promises.

If your pharmacy benefit currently feels like a black box, it doesn’t have to stay that way.

